ominalizer ~기 and reason marker 때문에. Finite verb → ~기 때문이다 (it is because). Often in written/formal contexts.", "ex_ko": "인공으로 만든 뉴런이 진짜 뇌세포와 신호를 주고받을 수 있다는 것이 입증되었기 때문입니다.", "ex_en": "This is because it has been proven that artificial neurons can exchange signals with real brain cells."}, {"name": "~다는 것", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Turns a whole statement into a noun: ''the fact that ~''. 주고받을 수 있다 → 주고받을 수 있다는 것 = the fact that they can exchange.", "ex_ko": "인공으로 만든 뉴런이 진짜 뇌세포와 신호를 주고받을 수 있다는 것이 입증되었기 때문입니다.", "ex_en": "This is because it has been proven that artificial neurons can exchange signals with real brain cells."}, {"name": "~다고 설명하다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Quotative ~다고 + speech verb 설명하다 (explain). Reported speech: finite clause → ~다고 + 설명하다.", "ex_ko": "연구진은 특수한 재료와 정밀한 기술을 활용했다고 설명했습니다.", "ex_en": "The research team explained that they utilized specialized materials and precision technology."}, {"name": "~ㄹ 것으로 기대되다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Future supposition ~ㄹ 것으로 + passive verb 기대되다. Marks expected/anticipated future action: 제시하다 → 제시할 것으로 기대되다.", "ex_ko": "이 기술은 향후 뇌 질환 치료에 새로운 가능성을 제시할 것으로 기대됩니다.", "ex_en": "This technology is expected to present new possibilities for treating brain diseases in the future."}, {"name": "~ 관련", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "관련 ''related to'' links two nouns directly. 뇌 관련 질병 = brain-related diseases.", "ex_ko": "파킨슨병이나 알츠하이머병 같은 뇌 관련 질병의 치료법 개발에 도움이 될 수 있습니다.", "ex_en": "It can help in the development of treatment methods for brain-related diseases such as Parkinson''s disease or Alzheimer''s disease."}, {"name": "~ㄴ (relative modifier on passive)", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Past relative clause modifier on passive verb: 손상되다 → 손상된 (damaged). Modifies the object 뇌세포.", "ex_ko": "손상된 뇌세포를 대체하거나 보완하는 치료가 가능해질 전망입니다.", "ex_en": "Treatments that replace or supplement damaged brain cells are expected to become possible."}, {"name": "~거나", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Connective ending meaning ''or'' between actions. 대체하다 → 대체하거나 보완하다 = to replace or supplement.", "ex_ko": "손상된 뇌세포를 대체하거나 보완하는 치료가 가능해질 전망입니다.", "ex_en": "Treatments that replace or supplement damaged brain cells are expected to become possible."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 전망이다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Formal news phrase meaning ''is expected to ~''. 가능해지다 → 가능해질 전망입니다 = is expected to become possible.", "ex_ko": "손상된 뇌세포를 대체하거나 보완하는 치료가 가능해질 전망입니다.", "ex_en": "Treatments that replace or supplement damaged brain cells are expected to become possible."}, {"name": "~이/가 될 것이다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Predicts a future state. 전환점이 되다 ''to become a turning point'' → 전환점이 될 것이다 = will become a turning point.", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 이번 연구가 미래 의학 기술의 새로운 전환점이 될 것이라고 평가했습니다.", "ex_en": "Experts assessed that this research would become a new turning point for future medical technology."}, {"name": "~(이)라고 평가하다", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Reports someone''s judgment. After 이다 the quote ending is ~라고: 될 것이다 → 될 것이라고 평가했습니다.", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 이번 연구가 미래 의학 기술의 새로운 전환점이 될 것이라고 평가했습니다.", "ex_en": "Experts assessed that this research would become a new turning point for future medical technology."}, {"name": "~까지는 (scope particle)", "level": "Advanced", "exp": "Particle ~까지는 marks a limit or boundary point. Here: until clinical application. Implies that further steps are needed beyond this point.", "ex_ko": "다만 실제 임상 적용까지는 더 많은 연구와 검증이 필요하다고 덧붙였습니다.", "ex_en": "However, they added that more research and verification are needed before actual clinical application."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moqehhca9gnx' and md5(translation) = 'aa8eb354d49daecedc622e2ba78d1eda';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A very special mask has been discovered in Germany. This mask appears to have been made around 1650, approximately 375 years ago.", "This mask was worn by \"plague doctors.\" When epidemics occurred, doctors wore masks like this to protect themselves. It is said that aromatic substances were placed in the long nose part of the mask.", "Currently, only two of these masks remain in the world. The mask discovered this time is one of them. It can be said to be a very valuable historical artifact.", "In Korea too, during the Joseon Dynasty when epidemics spread, doctors protected themselves using special methods. We can see that each country made efforts to prevent disease in different ways."], "sentences": [{"text": "독일에서 아주 특별한 가면이 발견됐어요.", "translation": "A very special mask was discovered in Germany.", "vocab": [{"ko": "독일", "en": "Germany", "note": "country name"}, {"ko": "발견되다", "en": "to be discovered", "note": "passive form of 발견하다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ/은/였어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Used with action verbs to express completed past actions or states in polite speech.", "example_in_sentence": "발견됐어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 가면은 약 375년 전인 1650년경에 만들어진 것으로 보여요.", "translation": "This mask appears to have been made around 1650, which was approximately 375 years ago.", "vocab": [{"ko": "약", "en": "approximately", "note": "used before numbers to express ''about'' or ''roughly''"}, {"ko": "만들어지다", "en": "to be made", "note": "passive form; can also mean ''to be created''"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~은/ㄴ 것으로 보이다", "exp": "Expresses a guess or inference based on observation or evidence.", "example_in_sentence": "만들어진 것으로 보여요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 가면은 ''전염병 의사''들이 썼던 것이에요.", "translation": "This mask is one that ''plague doctors'' used to wear.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전염병", "en": "plague/infectious disease", "note": "전염 (infection) + 병 (disease)"}, {"ko": "의사", "en": "doctor", "note": "medical professional"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~았던/었던", "exp": "Used to describe a past action or state that is no longer continuing.", "example_in_sentence": "썼던 것"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "전염병이 돌 때 의사들이 자신을 보호하기 위해 이런 가면을 썼어요.", "translation": "When plague spread, doctors wore such masks to protect themselves.", "vocab": [{"ko": "돌다", "en": "to spread/go around", "note": "used for diseases or rumors spreading"}, {"ko": "보호하다", "en": "to protect", "note": "transitive verb requiring an object"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~기 위해", "exp": "Indicates purpose or intention; means ''in order to'' or ''for the sake of''.", "example_in_sentence": "보호하기 위해"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "가면의 긴 코 부분에는 향료를 넣었다고 해요.", "translation": "It is said that fragrant substances were put in the long nose part of the mask.", "vocab": [{"ko": "향료", "en": "fragrance/scent", "note": "향 (scent) + 료 (materials)"}, {"ko": "넣다", "en": "to put/insert", "note": "common action verb"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~다고 하다", "exp": "Indirectly reports what someone said or what is believed; expresses hearsay.", "example_in_sentence": "넣었다고 해요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "현재 세계에 이런 가면은 단 두 개만 남아 있어요.", "translation": "Currently, only two such masks remain in the world.", "vocab": [{"ko": "현재", "en": "currently/at present", "note": "formal word for ''now''"}, {"ko": "남다", "en": "to remain/be left", "note": "intransitive verb"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이번에 발견된 가면이 그 중 하나예요.", "translation": "The mask discovered this time is one of those two.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이번", "en": "this time", "note": "이 (this) + 번 (time/turn)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~예요/이에요", "exp": "Polite copula expressing ''is/are''; used for identification or description.", "example_in_sentence": "그 중 하나예요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "매우 귀중한 역사 유물이라고 할 수 있어요.", "translation": "It can be said to be a very valuable historical artifact.", "vocab": [{"ko": "귀중하다", "en": "to be precious/valuable", "note": "adjective form; 귀 (precious) + 중 (important)"}, {"ko": "유물", "en": "artifact/relic", "note": "유 (remain) + 물 (thing)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~할 수 있다", "exp": "Expresses possibility or ability; can be said, can be done, etc.", "example_in_sentence": "할 수 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "한국에서도 조선시대에 전염병이 돌 때 의사들이 특별한 방법으로 자신을 보호했어요.", "translation": "In Korea, too, during the Joseon Dynasty when plague spread, doctors protected themselves through special methods.", "vocab": [{"ko": "조선시대", "en": "Joseon Dynasty", "note": "historical period of Korea (1392-1910)"}, {"ko": "방법", "en": "method/way", "note": "noun"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~도", "exp": "Particle meaning ''also'' or ''too''; shows inclusion or addition.", "example_in_sentence": "한국에서도"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "각 나라마다 다른 방식으로 병을 예방하려고 노력했다는 것을 알 수 있어요.", "translation": "We can see that each country tried to prevent disease in different ways.", "vocab": [{"ko": "각", "en": "each", "note": "나라 (country) + 마다 (each/every)"}, {"ko": "예방하다", "en": "to prevent", "note": "예 (prevention) + 방 (prevent) + 하다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~려고 하다", "exp": "Expresses intention or attempt to do something; ''try to'' or ''attempt to''.", "example_in_sentence": "예방하려고 노력했다"}, {"pattern": "~다는 것을 알 수 있다", "exp": "Expresses realization or understanding of a fact; ''can understand/see that''.", "example_in_sentence": "노력했다는 것을 알 수 있어요"}], "analysis": []}]}', vocab = '[{"ko": "독일", "en": "Germany", "note": "country name"}, {"ko": "발견되다", "en": "to be discovered", "note": "passive form of 발견하다"}, {"ko": "약", "en": "approximately", "note": "used before numbers to express ''about'' or ''roughly''"}, {"ko": "만들어지다", "en": "to be made", "note": "passive form; can also mean ''to be created''"}, {"ko": "전염병", "en": "plague/infectious disease", "note": "전염 (infection) + 병 (disease)"}, {"ko": "의사", "en": "doctor", "note": "medical professional"}, {"ko": "돌다", "en": "to spread/go around", "note": "used for diseases or rumors spreading"}, {"ko": "보호하다", "en": "to protect", "note": "transitive verb requiring an object"}, {"ko": "향료", "en": "fragrance/scent", "note": "향 (scent) + 료 (materials)"}, {"ko": "넣다", "en": "to put/insert", "note": "common action verb"}, {"ko": "현재", "en": "currently/at present", "note": "formal word for ''now''"}, {"ko": "남다", "en": "to remain/be left", "note": "intransitive verb"}, {"ko": "이번", "en": "this time", "note": "이 (this) + 번 (time/turn)"}, {"ko": "귀중하다", "en": "to be precious/valuable", "note": "adjective form; 귀 (precious) + 중 (important)"}, {"ko": "유물", "en": "artifact/relic", "note": "유 (remain) + 물 (thing)"}, {"ko": "조선시대", "en": "Joseon Dynasty", "note": "historical period of Korea (1392-1910)"}, {"ko": "방법", "en": "method/way", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "각", "en": "each", "note": "나라 (country) + 마다 (each/every)"}, {"ko": "예방하다", "en": "to prevent", "note": "예 (prevention) + 방 (prevent) + 하다"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moqq6skxfk4h' and md5(translation) = '3563110eee87120295b52cfecebb7e1b';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Zhangjiajie National Forest Park in Hunan Province, China is a world-famous tourist destination. This place is known for its towering pillar-shaped rock formations.", "These unique rock pillars are natural masterpieces created over hundreds of millions of years. The tallest rock exceeds 1,000 meters in height. When mist rolls in, they appear to be floating in the sky.", "The site became even more famous when it was used as the backdrop for the planet Pandora in the 2009 film Avatar. Since the movie''s filming, tourists from around the world have been flocking there.", "Many travelers from Korea are also visiting Zhangjiajie. It is particularly popular among younger generations as an Instagram photo spot. If you are planning a trip to China, it is definitely one of the places you should visit."], "sentences": [{"text": "중국 후난성에 있는 장가계 국가삼림공원은 세계적으로 유명한 관광지예요.", "translation": "Zhangjiajie National Forest Park in Hunan Province, China is a world-famous tourist destination.", "vocab": [{"ko": "후난성", "en": "Hunan Province", "note": "Chinese geographical location; 성 = province"}, {"ko": "국가삼림공원", "en": "national forest park", "note": "Compound noun: 국가(national) + 삼림(forest) + 공원(park)"}, {"ko": "세계적", "en": "global; worldwide", "note": "Adverb form with -적으로 suffix"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ/은 N (relative clause modifier)", "exp": "A past tense adjective modifies a noun; here ''있는'' (located) modifies ''장가계''", "example_in_sentence": "중국 후난성에 있는 장가계"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이곳은 높이 솟은 기둥 모양의 바위들로 유명해요.", "translation": "This place is famous for tall pillar-shaped rocks.", "vocab": [{"ko": "솟다", "en": "to soar; to rise", "note": "높이(height) + 솟다(to rise) in past tense"}, {"ko": "기둥 모양", "en": "pillar-shaped; column form", "note": "기둥(pillar/column) + 모양(shape)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄹ/을 기둥 모양의 바위들로 유명하다", "exp": "Expression ''~로 유명하다'' means ''to be famous for''; 로 marks the reason/cause", "example_in_sentence": "기둥 모양의 바위들로 유명해요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 독특한 바위 기둥들은 수억 년에 걸쳐 자연이 만든 작품이에요.", "translation": "These unique rock pillars are a masterpiece created by nature over hundreds of millions of years.", "vocab": [{"ko": "독특하다", "en": "unique; distinctive", "note": "Adjective commonly used for special features"}, {"ko": "수억 년", "en": "hundreds of millions of years", "note": "수(several) + 억(hundred million) + 년(year)"}, {"ko": "작품", "en": "work; masterpiece; creation", "note": "Often refers to artistic or creative outputs"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~에 걸쳐", "exp": "Means ''over (a period of time)''; indicates duration spanning", "example_in_sentence": "수억 년에 걸쳐"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "가장 높은 바위는 1,000미터가 넘어요.", "translation": "The highest rock exceeds 1,000 meters.", "vocab": [{"ko": "넘다", "en": "to exceed; to surpass; to go over", "note": "Used with numbers to show ''more than''"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~(이)가 1,000미터가 넘다", "exp": "Double subject construction; the thing (''가'') and the measure (''가'') both marked with 가", "example_in_sentence": "가장 높은 바위는 1,000미터가 넘어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "안개가 끼면 마치 하늘에 떠 있는 것처럼 보여요.", "translation": "When fog sets in, it looks as if it''s floating in the sky.", "vocab": [{"ko": "안개", "en": "fog; mist", "note": "Weather phenomenon"}, {"ko": "끼다", "en": "to set in; to envelop (of fog/clouds)", "note": "Specific to fog or clouds covering an area"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "마치 ~ㄴ 것처럼 보이다", "exp": "Expression meaning ''looks as if; looks like''; 마치 emphasizes ''as if''", "example_in_sentence": "마치 하늘에 떠 있는 것처럼 보여요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "2009년 영화 ''아바타''에서 판도라 행성의 배경으로 사용되면서 더욱 유명해졌어요.", "translation": "It became even more famous when it was used as the background for Pandora planet in the movie ''Avatar'' in 2009.", "vocab": [{"ko": "배경", "en": "background; setting", "note": "Common in film and art contexts"}, {"ko": "사용되다", "en": "to be used", "note": "Passive voice of 사용하다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~으면서 ~어지다", "exp": "Means ''and at the same time became''; shows simultaneous action and result", "example_in_sentence": "사용되면서 더욱 유명해졌어요"}, {"pattern": "~어/아지다", "exp": "Passive or stative verb meaning ''to become''; shows change of state", "example_in_sentence": "유명해졌어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "영화 촬영 이후 전 세계 관광객들이 몰려들고 있어요.", "translation": "Since the filming, tourists from all over the world have been flocking there.", "vocab": [{"ko": "촬영", "en": "filming; shooting (of a movie)", "note": "Used for photography/videography"}, {"ko": "이후", "en": "after; following", "note": "Formal/written form of 후에"}, {"ko": "몰려들다", "en": "to flock in; to crowd in", "note": "Expresses large numbers of people coming together"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect; indicates ongoing action in present", "example_in_sentence": "몰려들고 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "한국에서도 많은 여행객들이 장가계를 찾고 있어요.", "translation": "Many travelers from Korea are also visiting Zhangjiajie.", "vocab": [{"ko": "여행객", "en": "traveler; tourist", "note": "여행(travel) + 객(person; guest)"}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to visit; to seek; to find", "note": "In tourism context means ''to visit''"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "특히 젊은 세대들 사이에서 인스타그램 사진 촬영지로 인기가 높아요.", "translation": "Especially among young generations, it is popular as an Instagram photo-taking spot.", "vocab": [{"ko": "세대", "en": "generation; age group", "note": "Used in demographic contexts"}, {"ko": "사이", "en": "between; among", "note": "사이(between/among) + 에서(in/at)"}, {"ko": "촬영지", "en": "filming location; photo spot", "note": "촬영(filming) + 지(place)"}, {"ko": "인기", "en": "popularity", "note": "가 높다 = is high in popularity"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄹ/을 촬영지로 인기가 높다", "exp": "Expression structure: something is popular as [role]; 로 marks the function/role", "example_in_sentence": "인스타그램 사진 촬영지로 인기가 높아요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "중국 여행을 계획한다면 꼭 가봐야 할 곳 중 하나예요.", "translation": "If you plan a trip to China, it''s one of the must-see places.", "vocab": [{"ko": "계획하다", "en": "to plan", "note": "Common transitive verb"}, {"ko": "꼭", "en": "definitely; must; by all means", "note": "Adverb emphasizing necessity"}, {"ko": "가보다", "en": "to go and see; to visit", "note": "가다(go) + 보다(see); means to experience a place"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ다면 (conditional)", "exp": "Conditional form meaning ''if''; expresses hypothetical situation", "example_in_sentence": "중국 여행을 계획한다면"}, {"pattern": "~ㄹ 곳 중 하나", "exp": "Expression meaning ''one of the [places] to [do]''; indicates one option among many", "example_in_sentence": "꼭 가봐야 할 곳 중 하나예요"}], "analysis": []}]}', vocab = '[{"ko": "후난성", "en": "Hunan Province", "note": "Chinese geographical location; 성 = province"}, {"ko": "국가삼림공원", "en": "national forest park", "note": "Compound noun: 국가(national) + 삼림(forest) + 공원(park)"}, {"ko": "세계적", "en": "global; worldwide", "note": "Adverb form with -적으로 suffix"}, {"ko": "솟다", "en": "to soar; to rise", "note": "높이(height) + 솟다(to rise) in past tense"}, {"ko": "기둥 모양", "en": "pillar-shaped; column form", "note": "기둥(pillar/column) + 모양(shape)"}, {"ko": "독특하다", "en": "unique; distinctive", "note": "Adjective commonly used for special features"}, {"ko": "수억 년", "en": "hundreds of millions of years", "note": "수(several) + 억(hundred million) + 년(year)"}, {"ko": "작품", "en": "work; masterpiece; creation", "note": "Often refers to artistic or creative outputs"}, {"ko": "넘다", "en": "to exceed; to surpass; to go over", "note": "Used with numbers to show ''more than''"}, {"ko": "안개", "en": "fog; mist", "note": "Weather phenomenon"}, {"ko": "끼다", "en": "to set in; to envelop (of fog/clouds)", "note": "Specific to fog or clouds covering an area"}, {"ko": "배경", "en": "background; setting", "note": "Common in film and art contexts"}, {"ko": "사용되다", "en": "to be used", "note": "Passive voice of 사용하다"}, {"ko": "촬영", "en": "filming; shooting (of a movie)", "note": "Used for photography/videography"}, {"ko": "이후", "en": "after; following", "note": "Formal/written form of 후에"}, {"ko": "몰려들다", "en": "to flock in; to crowd in", "note": "Expresses large numbers of people coming together"}, {"ko": "여행객", "en": "traveler; tourist", "note": "여행(travel) + 객(person; guest)"}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to visit; to seek; to find", "note": "In tourism context means ''to visit''"}, {"ko": "세대", "en": "generation; age group", "note": "Used in demographic contexts"}, {"ko": "사이", "en": "between; among", "note": "사이(between/among) + 에서(in/at)"}, {"ko": "촬영지", "en": "filming location; photo spot", "note": "촬영(filming) + 지(place)"}, {"ko": "인기", "en": "popularity", "note": "가 높다 = is high in popularity"}, {"ko": "계획하다", "en": "to plan", "note": "Common transitive verb"}, {"ko": "꼭", "en": "definitely; must; by all means", "note": "Adverb emphasizing necessity"}, {"ko": "가보다", "en": "to go and see; to visit", "note": "가다(go) + 보다(see); means to experience a place"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moqq7sj41n19' and md5(translation) = '1c9390b5b6f52fd1c69a82bb0b320d61';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["What would a house cat do if it saw a tiger? Many people were curious about this.", "They actually brought a house cat in front of a tiger. The cat was very surprised at first. Its fur stood on end and it made its body small.", "But as time passed, things changed. The cat began to show interest in the tiger. It seemed like it felt that they were from the same cat family.", "Experts say this reaction is natural. This is because house cats and tigers originally have the same ancestor."], "sentences": [{"text": "집에서 기르는 고양이가 호랑이를 보면 어떻게 할까요?", "translation": "What would a cat raised at home do if it saw a tiger?", "vocab": [{"ko": "기르다", "en": "to raise, to keep (a pet)"}, {"ko": "호랑이", "en": "tiger"}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present participle modifier)", "exp": "Marks the preceding verb as a modifier describing the noun that follows. 기르다 → 기르는 (raising/that raises).", "example_in_sentence": "기르는 고양이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (conditional)", "exp": "Means ''if/when''. 보다 → 보면 = if (it) sees.", "example_in_sentence": "보면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ까요?", "exp": "Asks a wondering question: ''What would it do?'' 하다 → 할까요?", "example_in_sentence": "어떻게 할까요?"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 궁금해했어요.", "translation": "Many people were curious about it.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; to be a lot"}, {"ko": "궁금해하다", "en": "to be curious; to wonder"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Polite past tense ending. 궁금해하다 → 궁금해했어요 = were curious.", "example_in_sentence": "궁금해했어요"}]}, {"text": "실제로 집 고양이를 호랑이 앞에 데려갔어요.", "translation": "Someone actually brought a house cat in front of a tiger.", "vocab": [{"ko": "실제로", "en": "actually, in reality"}, {"ko": "데려가다", "en": "to take (someone) along, to bring"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Marks completed action. 데려가다 → 데려갔어요 (brought).", "example_in_sentence": "데려갔어요"}]}, {"text": "고양이는 처음에 매우 놀랐어요.", "translation": "The cat was very surprised at first.", "vocab": [{"ko": "처음에", "en": "at first, initially"}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very, greatly"}, {"ko": "놀라다", "en": "to be surprised, to be startled"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Marks completed action. 놀라다 → 놀랐어요 (was surprised).", "example_in_sentence": "놀랐어요"}]}, {"text": "털이 곤두서고 몸을 작게 만들었어요.", "translation": "[Its] fur stood on end and [it] made [its] body small.", "vocab": [{"ko": "털", "en": "fur, hair"}, {"ko": "곤두서다", "en": "to stand on end (of hair/fur)"}, {"ko": "몸", "en": "body"}, {"ko": "작다", "en": "to be small"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 (conjunctive ending)", "exp": "Connects two predicates in sequence, indicating parallel or sequential actions. 곤두서다 → 곤두서고 (stood on end and).", "example_in_sentence": "곤두서고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 만들다 (causative expression)", "exp": "Means ''to make [something] [adjective]''. 작다 → 작게 (small [way]) + 만들다 (make).", "example_in_sentence": "작게 만들었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Marks completed action. 만들다 → 만들었어요 (made).", "example_in_sentence": "만들었어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 시간이 지나면서 달라졌어요.", "translation": "But as time passed, [it] changed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "but, however"}, {"ko": "시간", "en": "time"}, {"ko": "지나다", "en": "to pass, to go by"}, {"ko": "달라지다", "en": "to change, to become different"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면서 (while/as)", "exp": "Shows two things happening together. 지나다 → 지나면서 = as (time) passed.", "example_in_sentence": "지나면서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Marks completed action. 달라지다 → 달라졌어요 (changed).", "example_in_sentence": "달라졌어요"}]}, {"text": "고양이는 호랑이에게 관심을 보이기 시작했어요.", "translation": "The cat began to show interest in the tiger.", "vocab": [{"ko": "관심", "en": "interest"}, {"ko": "보이다", "en": "to show"}, {"ko": "시작하다", "en": "to begin, to start"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 시작하다 (aspect: inchoative)", "exp": "Marks the beginning of an action. 보이다 → 보이기 (showing) + 시작하다 (began).", "example_in_sentence": "보이기 시작했어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Marks completed action. 시작하다 → 시작했어요 (began).", "example_in_sentence": "시작했어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "관심을 보이다 (to show interest)", "exp": "Fixed collocation meaning ''to demonstrate or express interest''. Direct object 관심 (interest) + 보이다 (show).", "example_in_sentence": "관심을 보이기"}]}, {"text": "같은 고양이 가족이라는 것을 느낀 것 같았어요.", "translation": "It seemed to feel that they were part of the same cat family.", "vocab": [{"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same"}, {"ko": "가족", "en": "family"}, {"ko": "느끼다", "en": "to feel"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ 것 같다 (conjecture/appearance)", "exp": "Expresses conjecture or appearance: ''[it] seemed/appeared to have''. 느끼다 → 느낀 (felt) + 것 (fact/thing) + 같다 (seemed).", "example_in_sentence": "느낀 것 같았어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~라는 것 (nominalization: ''the fact/thing that'')", "exp": "Nominalizes a clause. 가족이다 → 가족이라는 (the fact that [they are] family).", "example_in_sentence": "가족이라는 것을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Marks completed state. 같다 → 같았어요 (seemed).", "example_in_sentence": "같았어요"}]}, {"text": "전문가들은 이런 반응이 자연스럽다고 말해요.", "translation": "Experts say that such a reaction is natural.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert, specialist"}, {"ko": "반응", "en": "reaction, response"}, {"ko": "자연스럽다", "en": "to be natural"}, {"ko": "말하다", "en": "to say, to speak"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 말하다 (reported speech)", "exp": "Marks indirect quotation. 자연스럽다 → 자연스럽다고 (that [it] is natural) + 말하다 (say).", "example_in_sentence": "자연스럽다고 말해요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어요 (present tense, polite)", "exp": "Marks habitual or general present. 말하다 → 말해요 (say).", "example_in_sentence": "말해요"}]}, {"text": "집 고양이와 호랑이는 원래 같은 조상을 가지고 있거든요.", "translation": "After all, domestic cats and tigers originally have the same ancestor.", "vocab": [{"ko": "원래", "en": "originally, in the first place"}, {"ko": "조상", "en": "ancestor"}, {"ko": "가지다", "en": "to have, to possess"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (progressive/state)", "exp": "Marks ongoing state or possession. 가지다 → 가지고 있다 (have/possess in an ongoing state).", "example_in_sentence": "가지고 있거든요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~거든요 (explanatory ending)", "exp": "Provides explanation or reason with emphasis. Often used with present state to justify preceding statement.", "example_in_sentence": "있거든요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "기르다", "en": "to raise, to keep (a pet)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "호랑이", "en": "tiger", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; to be a lot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "궁금해하다", "en": "to be curious; to wonder", "note": ""}, {"ko": "실제로", "en": "actually, in reality", "note": ""}, {"ko": "데려가다", "en": "to take (someone) along, to bring", "note": ""}, {"ko": "처음에", "en": "at first, initially", "note": ""}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very, greatly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀라다", "en": "to be surprised, to be startled", "note": ""}, {"ko": "털", "en": "fur, hair", "note": ""}, {"ko": "곤두서다", "en": "to stand on end (of hair/fur)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "몸", "en": "body", "note": ""}, {"ko": "작다", "en": "to be small", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하지만", "en": "but, however", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시간", "en": "time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지나다", "en": "to pass, to go by", "note": ""}, {"ko": "달라지다", "en": "to change, to become different", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관심", "en": "interest", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보이다", "en": "to show", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시작하다", "en": "to begin, to start", "note": ""}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가족", "en": "family", "note": ""}, {"ko": "느끼다", "en": "to fe