 + 만들다 (make).", "ex_ko": "털이 곤두서고 몸을 작게 만들었어요.", "ex_en": "[Its] fur stood on end and [it] made [its] body small."}, {"name": "~기 시작하다 (aspect: inchoative)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks the beginning of an action. 보이다 → 보이기 (showing) + 시작하다 (began).", "ex_ko": "고양이는 호랑이에게 관심을 보이기 시작했어요.", "ex_en": "The cat began to show interest in the tiger."}, {"name": "~ㄴ 것 같다 (conjecture/appearance)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Expresses conjecture or appearance: ''[it] seemed/appeared to have''. 느끼다 → 느낀 (felt) + 것 (fact/thing) + 같다 (seemed).", "ex_ko": "같은 고양이 가족이라는 것을 느낀 것 같았어요.", "ex_en": "It seemed to feel that they were part of the same cat family."}, {"name": "~라는 것 (nominalization: ''the fact/thing that'')", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Nominalizes a clause. 가족이다 → 가족이라는 (the fact that [they are] family).", "ex_ko": "같은 고양이 가족이라는 것을 느낀 것 같았어요.", "ex_en": "It seemed to feel that they were part of the same cat family."}, {"name": "~다고 말하다 (reported speech)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks indirect quotation. 자연스럽다 → 자연스럽다고 (that [it] is natural) + 말하다 (say).", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 이런 반응이 자연스럽다고 말해요.", "ex_en": "Experts say that such a reaction is natural."}, {"name": "~어요 (present tense, polite)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks habitual or general present. 말하다 → 말해요 (say).", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 이런 반응이 자연스럽다고 말해요.", "ex_en": "Experts say that such a reaction is natural."}, {"name": "~고 있다 (progressive/state)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks ongoing state or possession. 가지다 → 가지고 있다 (have/possess in an ongoing state).", "ex_ko": "집 고양이와 호랑이는 원래 같은 조상을 가지고 있거든요.", "ex_en": "After all, domestic cats and tigers originally have the same ancestor."}, {"name": "~거든요 (explanatory ending)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Provides explanation or reason with emphasis. Often used with present state to justify preceding statement.", "ex_ko": "집 고양이와 호랑이는 원래 같은 조상을 가지고 있거든요.", "ex_en": "After all, domestic cats and tigers originally have the same ancestor."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mor0uzqmtzd1' and md5(translation) = '82158f43cf93658842a4be4b453b2ea8';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A passenger in the United States prevented a plane from departing. This passenger did not hang up the phone before the plane was supposed to take off.", "Flight attendants told the passenger to hang up the phone several times. However, this passenger continued to make calls. Other passengers also had to wait.", "Eventually, the plane stopped preparing for departure and returned to the airport. This passenger had to get off the plane.", "On an airplane, you must follow the rules for safety. If you don''t listen to the flight attendants, it can cause a big problem."], "sentences": [{"text": "미국에서 한 승객 때문에 비행기가 출발하지 못했어요.", "translation": "In the U.S., a plane couldn''t take off because of one passenger.", "vocab": [{"ko": "승객", "en": "passenger", "note": "Common TOPIK word for airplane/public transport contexts"}, {"ko": "때문에", "en": "because of / due to", "note": "Shows cause; 명사 + 때문에"}, {"ko": "출발하다", "en": "to depart", "note": "Opposite: 도착하다 (arrive)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~지 못했어요", "exp": "Negative past tense meaning ''was unable to'' or ''couldn''t''; expresses inability or failure", "example_in_sentence": "비행기가 출발하지 못했어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 승객은 비행기가 출발하기 전에 전화를 끊지 않았어요.", "translation": "This passenger did not hang up the phone before the airplane departed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전화를 끊다", "en": "to hang up (a phone call)", "note": "끊다 = to cut/hang up; 전화 = telephone"}, {"ko": "전에", "en": "before", "note": "Temporal marker; 동사 + 기 전에"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~기 전에", "exp": "Expresses ''before doing [verb]''; marks the time point prior to an action", "example_in_sentence": "비행기가 출발하기 전에"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "비행기 승무원들이 여러 번 전화를 끊으라고 말했어요.", "translation": "Flight attendants told [the passenger] to hang up the phone several times.", "vocab": [{"ko": "승무원", "en": "flight attendant / crew member", "note": "승무 = crew; 원 = person"}, {"ko": "여러 번", "en": "several times / multiple times", "note": "여러 = several; 번 = times/occasions"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~으라고 말하다", "exp": "Reports a command or instruction; ''told/said to [do something]''", "example_in_sentence": "전화를 끊으라고 말했어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "하지만 이 승객은 계속 전화를 했어요.", "translation": "But this passenger kept calling.", "vocab": [{"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously / to keep doing", "note": "Adverb; 계속 + 동사"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "다른 승객들도 기다려야 했어요.", "translation": "Other passengers also had to wait.", "vocab": [{"ko": "다른", "en": "different / other", "note": "Adjective; 다른 + 명사"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~아/어야 했어요", "exp": "Past obligation or necessity; ''had to / was obliged to''", "example_in_sentence": "기다려야 했어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "결국 비행기는 출발 준비를 멈추고 다시 공항으로 돌아갔어요.", "translation": "In the end, the airplane stopped preparing to depart and went back to the airport.", "vocab": [{"ko": "결국", "en": "in the end / finally / after all", "note": "Adverb expressing final outcome"}, {"ko": "준비", "en": "preparation", "note": "준비를 하다 = to prepare; 준비를 멈추다 = to stop preparing"}, {"ko": "돌아가다", "en": "to return / to go back", "note": "Opposite of 나가다 (go out)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고", "exp": "Connects two sequential or parallel actions; ''and then / and''", "example_in_sentence": "멈추고 다시 공항으로 돌아갔어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 승객은 비행기에서 내려야 했어요.", "translation": "This passenger had to get off the airplane.", "vocab": [{"ko": "내리다", "en": "to get off / to descend", "note": "탑승 (board) vs 하차 (disembark); ~에서 내리다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~아/어야 했어요", "exp": "Past obligation; ''had to / was forced to''", "example_in_sentence": "내려야 했어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "비행기에서는 안전을 위해 규칙을 지켜야 해요.", "translation": "On an airplane, [people] must follow rules for safety.", "vocab": [{"ko": "안전", "en": "safety", "note": "안전하다 (to be safe); 안전 + 을/를 위해"}, {"ko": "규칙", "en": "rule / regulation", "note": "규칙을 지키다 = to follow rules"}, {"ko": "지키다", "en": "to keep / to follow / to observe", "note": "규칙을 지키다, 약속을 지키다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~아/어야 해요", "exp": "Present obligation or necessity; ''must / have to / should''", "example_in_sentence": "규칙을 지켜야 해요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "승무원의 말을 듣지 않으면 큰 문제가 될 수 있어요.", "translation": "If [people] don''t listen to the flight attendant, it can become a big problem.", "vocab": [{"ko": "문제", "en": "problem / issue", "note": "문제가 생기다 = a problem arises"}, {"ko": "되다", "en": "to become", "note": "Expresses possibility; ~ㄹ 수 있다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~으면", "exp": "Conditional ''if''; expresses a hypothetical condition and result", "example_in_sentence": "말을 듣지 않으면"}], "analysis": []}]}', vocab = '[{"ko": "승객", "en": "passenger", "note": "Common TOPIK word for airplane/public transport contexts"}, {"ko": "때문에", "en": "because of / due to", "note": "Shows cause; 명사 + 때문에"}, {"ko": "출발하다", "en": "to depart", "note": "Opposite: 도착하다 (arrive)"}, {"ko": "전화를 끊다", "en": "to hang up (a phone call)", "note": "끊다 = to cut/hang up; 전화 = telephone"}, {"ko": "전에", "en": "before", "note": "Temporal marker; 동사 + 기 전에"}, {"ko": "승무원", "en": "flight attendant / crew member", "note": "승무 = crew; 원 = person"}, {"ko": "여러 번", "en": "several times / multiple times", "note": "여러 = several; 번 = times/occasions"}, {"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously / to keep doing", "note": "Adverb; 계속 + 동사"}, {"ko": "다른", "en": "different / other", "note": "Adjective; 다른 + 명사"}, {"ko": "결국", "en": "in the end / finally / after all", "note": "Adverb expressing final outcome"}, {"ko": "준비", "en": "preparation", "note": "준비를 하다 = to prepare; 준비를 멈추다 = to stop preparing"}, {"ko": "돌아가다", "en": "to return / to go back", "note": "Opposite of 나가다 (go out)"}, {"ko": "내리다", "en": "to get off / to descend", "note": "탑승 (board) vs 하차 (disembark); ~에서 내리다"}, {"ko": "안전", "en": "safety", "note": "안전하다 (to be safe); 안전 + 을/를 위해"}, {"ko": "규칙", "en": "rule / regulation", "note": "규칙을 지키다 = to follow rules"}, {"ko": "지키다", "en": "to keep / to follow / to observe", "note": "규칙을 지키다, 약속을 지키다"}, {"ko": "문제", "en": "problem / issue", "note": "문제가 생기다 = a problem arises"}, {"ko": "되다", "en": "to become", "note": "Expresses possibility; ~ㄹ 수 있다"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mor0vmsrk0rr' and md5(translation) = '64c44fe8073641175e2d0c81e72b43bf';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "1963년 미국 야구 선수 게일로드 페리가 재미있는 말을 했어요.", "idx": 0, "translation": "In 1963, American baseball player Gaylord Perry said something interesting.", "vocab": [{"ko": "야구 선수", "en": "baseball player", "note": "compound noun"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ/은 명사", "exp": "descriptive modifying clause before a noun", "example_in_sentence": "재미있는 말"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "\"사람이 달에 가기 전에는 내가 홈런을 칠 수 없을 거야\"라고 농담을 했습니다.", "idx": 1, "translation": "He joked, \"I won''t be able to hit a home run before humans go to the moon.\"", "vocab": [{"ko": "농담하다", "en": "to joke"}, {"ko": "홈런", "en": "home run"}, {"ko": "달", "en": "moon"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~기 전에", "exp": "before doing something", "example_in_sentence": "달에 가기 전에"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "페리는 투수(공을 던지는 선수)였어요.", "idx": 2, "translation": "Perry was a pitcher (a player who throws the ball).", "vocab": [{"ko": "투수", "en": "pitcher"}, {"ko": "던지다", "en": "to throw"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "투수는 보통 홈런을 잘 치지 못해서 이런 말을 한 거였어요.", "idx": 3, "translation": "Since pitchers usually can''t hit home runs well, he made such a remark.", "vocab": [{"ko": "보통", "en": "usually"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~아서/어서", "exp": "because; so (cause-effect)", "example_in_sentence": "잘 치지 못해서"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "1969년 7월 20일, 닐 암스트롱이 인류 최초로 달에 발을 디뎠어요.", "idx": 4, "translation": "On July 20, 1969, Neil Armstrong became the first human to set foot on the moon.", "vocab": [{"ko": "최초", "en": "first; earliest"}, {"ko": "발을 디디다", "en": "to step on; to set foot on"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그런데 놀라운 일이 일어났습니다.", "idx": 5, "translation": "But something surprising happened.", "vocab": [{"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising; to be astonishing"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "암스트롱이 달에 간 지 한 시간 후에 페리가 정말로 홈런을 쳤어요.", "idx": 6, "translation": "An hour after Armstrong went to the moon, Perry actually hit a home run.", "vocab": [], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ 지 시간 후에", "exp": "after time has passed since an event", "example_in_sentence": "달에 간 지 한 시간 후에"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이것은 그의 생애 첫 번째이자 마지막 홈런이었습니다.", "idx": 7, "translation": "This was his first and last home run in his lifetime.", "vocab": [{"ko": "생애", "en": "lifetime; one''s life"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ/은 것이다", "exp": "it was (copular emphasis)", "example_in_sentence": "마지막 홈런이었습니다"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "6년 전 농담이 그대로 현실이 된 신기한 하루였어요.", "idx": 8, "translation": "It was a miraculous day when a joke from six years before became reality exactly as stated.", "vocab": [{"ko": "신기하다", "en": "amazing; miraculous"}, {"ko": "그대로", "en": "exactly as; just as it was"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ/은 것이 현실이 되다", "exp": "something becomes reality", "example_in_sentence": "농담이 그대로 현실이 된"}], "analysis": []}]}', vocab = '[{"ko": "야구 선수", "en": "baseball player", "note": "compound noun"}, {"ko": "농담하다", "en": "to joke", "note": ""}, {"ko": "홈런", "en": "home run", "note": ""}, {"ko": "달", "en": "moon", "note": ""}, {"ko": "투수", "en": "pitcher", "note": ""}, {"ko": "던지다", "en": "to throw", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보통", "en": "usually", "note": ""}, {"ko": "최초", "en": "first; earliest", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발을 디디다", "en": "to step on; to set foot on", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising; to be astonishing", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생애", "en": "lifetime; one''s life", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "amazing; miraculous", "note": ""}, {"ko": "그대로", "en": "exactly as; just as it was", "note": ""}, {"word": "인류", "reading": "inryyu", "meaning": "humankind; humanity; mankind", "context": "닐 암스트롱이 인류 최초로 달에 발을 디뎠어요."}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mor0wfixgfqn' and md5(translation) = '956f1c1adc6754832fb105b5bf9e3c4c';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Giardia lamblia is a small parasite. This parasite lives in the small intestine of humans. When infected with giardia, you get diarrhea. This diarrhea smells very bad. It''s also characterized by being oily. This parasite enters your body when you drink dirty water. You can become infected even if you don''t wash your hands thoroughly. If you catch giardia, you need to go to the hospital. When a doctor gives you medicine, you can get better. It''s important to wash your hands frequently on a regular basis.", "Korean teacher shortage crisis worsens, disrupting school classes", "What is an ''anxiety bag''? A popular trend", "The US and China resume talks over trade issues", "\"Talking pig\" becomes an SNS star", "''Nothing maxing'' trend spreads—doing absolutely nothing"], "sentences": [{"text": "지아디아 람블리아(Giardia lamblia)는 작은 기생충이에요.", "translation": "Giardia lamblia is a small parasite.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기생충", "en": "parasite"}, {"ko": "작다", "en": "to be small"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이에요", "exp": "Copula (present tense declarative form for 이다). Attaches to noun to make statement: 기생충(noun) + 이에요 = is a parasite.", "example_in_sentence": "기생충이에요"}]}, {"text": "이 기생충은 사람의 소장에서 살아요.", "translation": "This parasite lives in the human small intestine.", "vocab": [{"ko": "소장", "en": "small intestine"}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Location/source particle marking where an action takes place. 소장(location) + 에서 = in the small intestine.", "example_in_sentence": "소장에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요", "exp": "Present tense informal declarative ending. 살(verb stem) + 아요 = lives (present).", "example_in_sentence": "살아요"}]}, {"text": "지아디아에 감염되면 설사를 해요.", "translation": "If infected with giardia, one has diarrhea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "감염되다", "en": "to be infected"}, {"ko": "설사", "en": "diarrhea"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면", "exp": "Means ''if/when''. 감염되다 → 감염되면 = if (you) get infected.", "example_in_sentence": "감염되면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 하다", "exp": "Light verb construction where 하다 combines with object noun. 설사(noun) + 를(object marker) + 해요 = has/does diarrhea.", "example_in_sentence": "설사를 해요"}]}, {"text": "이 설사는 냄새가 매우 나빠요.", "translation": "This diarrhea has a very bad smell.", "vocab": [{"ko": "냄새", "en": "smell; odor"}, {"ko": "나쁘다", "en": "to be bad"}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very; extremely"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~가", "exp": "Subject marker highlighting the attribute being described. 냄새(subject) + 가 = the smell (as the subject of the predicate).", "example_in_sentence": "냄새가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요", "exp": "Present tense informal declarative. 나쁘(adjective stem) + 아요 = is bad.", "example_in_sentence": "나빠요"}]}, {"text": "기름기가 많은 것도 특징이에요.", "translation": "Being greasy is also a characteristic.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기름기", "en": "greasiness; oiliness"}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; to be much"}, {"ko": "특징", "en": "characteristic; feature"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 것", "exp": "Turns a description into a noun phrase. 많다 → 많은 것 = (the fact of) having a lot.", "example_in_sentence": "많은 것"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "Additive particle meaning ''also; too''. 것(noun) + 도 = is also a characteristic.", "example_in_sentence": "것도"}]}, {"text": "이 기생충은 더러운 물을 마실 때 몸에 들어와요.", "translation": "This parasite enters the body when one drinks dirty water.", "vocab": [{"ko": "더럽다", "en": "to be dirty"}, {"ko": "마시다", "en": "to drink"}, {"ko": "들어오다", "en": "to enter; to come in"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 때", "exp": "Means ''when ~''. 마시다 → 마실 때 = when (someone) drinks.", "example_in_sentence": "마실 때"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "Direction/destination particle. 몸(destination) + 에 = into the body.", "example_in_sentence": "몸에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요", "exp": "Present tense. 들어오(verb stem) + 아요 = enters.", "example_in_sentence": "들어와요"}]}, {"text": "손을 깨끗하게 씻지 않아도 감염될 수 있어요.", "translation": "One can become infected even without washing hands cleanly.", "vocab": [{"ko": "깨끗하다", "en": "to be clean"}, {"ko": "씻다", "en": "to wash"}, {"ko": "감염되다", "en": "to be infected"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "Negation suffix. 씻(verb) + 지 않다 = not wash.", "example_in_sentence": "씻지 않아도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어도", "exp": "Connective ending meaning ''even if''. 않다 → 않아도 = even if (you) don''t.", "example_in_sentence": "않아도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Means ''can / might''. 감염되다 → 감염될 수 있어요 = can get infected.", "example_in_sentence": "감염될 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "지아디아에 걸리면 병원에 가야 해요.", "translation": "If one catches giardia, one must go to the hospital.", "vocab": [{"ko": "걸리다", "en": "to catch (a disease)"}, {"ko": "병원", "en": "hospital"}, {"ko": "가다", "en": "to go"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면", "exp": "Means ''if/when''. 걸리다 → 걸리면 = if (you) catch it.", "example_in_sentence": "걸리면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어야 하다", "exp": "Expresses obligation: ''must / have to''. 가다 → 가야 해요 = must go.", "example_in_sentence": "가야 해요"}]}, {"text": "의사가 약을 주면 나을 수 있어요.", "translation": "If a doctor gives medicine, one can recover.", "vocab": [{"ko": "의사", "en": "doctor"}, {"ko": "약", "en": "medicine; drug"}, {"ko": "낫다", "en": "to recover; to get better"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면", "exp": "Means ''if/when''. 주다 → 주면 = if (a doctor) gives.", "example_in_sentence": "주면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Means ''can''. 낫다 is irregular: the ㅅ drops before 으, so 낫다 → 나을 수 있어요 = can recover.", "example_in_sentence": "나을 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "평소에 손을 자주 씻는 것이 중요해요.", "translation": "It is important to wash your hands often in daily life.", "vocab": [{"ko": "평소", "en": "usually; normally; ordinarily"}, {"ko": "자주", "en": "frequently; often"}, {"ko": "씻다", "en": "to wash"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것", "exp": "Turns a verb into a noun: ''the act of ~ing''. 씻다 → 씻는 것 = washing.", "example_in_sentence": "씻는 것"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "Subject marker. 것(subject) + 이 = (the washing) is important.", "example_in_sentence": "것이"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "기생충", "en": "parasite", "note": ""}, {"ko": "작다", "en": "to be small", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소장", "en": "small intestine", "note": ""}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live", "note": ""}, {"ko": "감염되다", "en": "to be infected", "note": ""}, {"ko": "설사", "en": "diarrhea", "note": ""}, {"ko": "냄새", "en": "smell; odor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나쁘다", "en": "to be bad", "note": ""}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very; extremely", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기름기", "en": "greasiness; oiliness", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; to be much", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특징", "en": "characteristic; feature", "note": ""}, {"ko": "더럽다", "en": "to be dirty", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마시다", "en": "to drink", "note": ""}, {"ko": "들어오다", "en": "to enter; to come in", "note": ""}, {"ko": "깨끗하다", "en": "to be clean", "note": ""}, {"ko": "씻다", "en": "to wash", "note": ""}, {"ko": "걸리다", "en": "to catch (a disease)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "병원", "en": "hospital", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가다", "en": "to go", "note": ""}, {"ko": "의사", "en": "doctor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "약", "en": "medicine; drug", "note": ""}, {"ko": "낫다", "en": "to recover; to get better", "note": ""}, {"ko": "평소", "en": "usually; normally; ordinarily", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자주", "en": "frequently; often", "note": ""}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~이에요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Copula (present tense declarative form for 이다). Attaches to noun to make statement: 기생충(noun) + 이에요 = is a parasite.", "ex_ko": "지아디아 람블리아(Giardia lamblia)는 작은 기생충이에요.", "ex_en": "Giardia lamblia is a small parasite."}, {"name": "~에서", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Location/source particle marking where an action takes place. 소장(location) + 에서 = in the small intestine.", "ex_ko": "이 기생충은 사람의 소장에서 살아요.", "ex_en": "This parasite lives in the human small intestine."}, {"name": "~아/어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Present tense informal declarative ending. 살(verb stem) + 아요 = lives (present).", "ex_ko": "이 기생충은 사람의 소장에서 살아요.", "ex_en": "This parasite lives in the human small intestine."}, {"name": "~(으)면", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''if/when''. 감염되다 → 감염되면 = if (you) get infected.", "ex_ko": "지아디아에 감염되면 설사를 해요.", "ex_en": "If infected with giardia, one has diarrhea."}, {"name": "~을/를 하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Light verb construction where 하다 combines with object noun. 설사(noun) + 를(object marker) + 해요 = has/does diarrhea.", "ex_ko": "지아디아에 감염되면 설사를 해요.", "ex_en": "If infected with giardia, one has diarrhea."}, {"name": "~가", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Subject marker highlighting the attribute being described. 냄새(subject) + 가 = the smell (as the subject of the predicate).", "ex_ko": "이 설사는 냄새가 매우 나빠요.", "ex_en": "This diarrhea has a very bad smell."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 것", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Turns a description into a noun phrase. 많다 → 많은 것 = (the fact of) having a lot.", "ex_ko": "기름기가 많은 것도 특징이에요.", "ex_en": "Being greasy is also a characteristic."}, {"name": "~도", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Additive particle meaning ''also; too''. 것(noun) + 도 = is also a characteristic.", "ex_ko": "기름기가 많은 것도 특징이에요.", "ex_en": "Being greasy is also a characteristic."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 때", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''when ~''. 마시다 → 마실 때 = when (someone) drinks.", "ex_ko": "이 기생충은 더러운 물을 마실 때 몸에 들어와요.", "ex_en": "This parasite enters the body when one drinks dirty water."}, {"name": "~지 않다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Negation suffix. 씻(verb) + 지 않다 = not wash.", "ex_ko": "손을 깨끗하게 씻지 않아도 감염될 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "One can become infected even without washing hands cleanly."}, {"name": "~아/어도", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Connective ending meaning ''even if''. 않다 → 않아도 = even if (you) don''t.", "ex_ko": "손을 깨끗하게 씻지 않아도 감염될 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "One can become infected even without washing hands cleanly."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''can''. 낫다 is irregular: the ㅅ drops before 으, so 낫다 → 나을 수 있어요 = can recover.", "ex_ko": "손을 깨끗하게 씻지 않아도 감염될 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "One can become infected even without washing hands cleanly."}, {"name": "~아/어야 하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Expresses obligation: ''must / have to''. 가다 → 가야 해요 = must go.", "ex_ko": "지아디아에 걸리면 병원에 가야 해요.", "ex_en": "If one catches giardia, one must go to the hospital."}, {"name": "~는 것", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Turns a verb into a noun: ''the act of ~ing''. 씻다 → 씻는 것 = washing.", "ex_ko": "평소에 손을 자주 씻는 것이 중요해요.", "ex_en": "It is important to wash your hands often in daily life."}, {"name": "~이/가", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Subject marker. 것(subject) + 이 = (the washing) is important.", "ex_ko": "평소에 손을 자주 씻는 것이 중요해요.", "ex_en": "It is important to wash your hands often in daily life."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mor0x3udjeta' and md5(translation) = '66bbae537721c4dc16a41c1dec79fe45';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A building in Moscow, the capital of Russia, was attacked by a drone. This building is located several kilometers away from the Kremlin.", "The Kremlin is where the Russian president works. Therefore, this attack is considered a very sensitive matter. Russian authorities have launched an investigation into the incident.", "It is uncommon for such attacks to occur near the center of Moscow. The international community is also closely monitoring this situation.", "South Korea''s Ministry of Foreign Affairs has not yet issued an official statement regarding this incident. However, it is said that they continue to observe changes in the international situation."], "sentences": [{"text": "러시아 수도 모스크바의 한 건물이 드론(무인기) 공격을 받았어요.", "translation": "A building in Moscow, the capital of Russia, was attacked by a drone.", "vocab": [{"ko": "수도", "en": "capital (city)", "note": "Used with place names to indicate the main city of a country"}, {"ko": "드론", "en": "drone", "note": "Loanword; also called 무인기 (unmanned aircraft)"}, {"ko": "공격을 받다", "en": "to be attacked", "note": "Passive construction: literally ''receive an attack''"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ/은 (noun modifier)", "exp": "Transforms a verb or adjective into a modifier for the noun that follows.", "example_in_sentence": "러시아 수도 모스크바"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 건물은 크렘린궁에서 몇 킬로미터 떨어진 곳에 있어요.", "translation": "This building is located several kilometers away from the Kremlin.", "vocab": [{"ko": "떨어지다", "en": "to be (located) away; to be distant", "note": "Past participle form of 떨어지다; modifies the noun 곳"}, {"ko": "킬로미터", "en": "kilometer", "note": "Loanword for metric distance unit"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ/은 곳에 있다", "exp": "Describes the location of something using a modified noun phrase with 곳.", "example_in_sentence": "크렘린궁에서 몇 킬로미터 떨어진 곳에 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "크렘린궁은 러시아 대통령이 일하는 곳이에요.", "translation": "The Kremlin is where the Russian president works.", "vocab": [{"ko": "크렘린궁", "en": "the Kremlin", "note": "Proper noun; Russian presidential complex"}, {"ko": "대통령", "en": "president", "note": "Head of state in a country"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~는 곳이다", "exp": "Identifies or defines a place: ''the place where [verb]''.", "example_in_sentence": "러시아 대통령이 일하는 곳이에요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "따라서 이번 공격은 매우 민감한 사안으로 여겨져요.", "translation": "Therefore, this attack is considered a very sensitive matter.", "vocab": [{"ko": "민감하다", "en": "to be sensitive; to be delicate", "note": "Adjective describing topics that require caution"}, {"ko": "사안", "en": "matter; issue; case", "note": "Formal noun for a specific situation or problem"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~(으)로 여겨지다", "exp": "Passive form meaning ''to be considered/regarded as''; expresses what something is thought to be.", "example_in_sentence": "매우 민감한 사안으로 여겨져요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "러시아 당국은 사건 조사에 나섰어요.", "translation": "Russian authorities have launched an investigation into the incident.", "vocab": [{"ko": "당국", "en": "authorities", "note": "Official government bodies or officials"}, {"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; case; event", "note": "Used for significant events, accidents, or crimes"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~에 나서다", "exp": "Means ''to set out to; to take action on''; often used for initiatives or investigations.", "example_in_sentence": "사건 조사에 나섰어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이런 공격이 모스크바 중심부 근처에서 일어난 것은 흔하지 않은 일이에요.", "translation": "It is uncommon for such attacks to occur near the center of Moscow.", "vocab": [{"ko": "흔하다", "en": "to be common (흔하지 않다 = uncommon)", "note": "Negated form of 흔하다; indicates something is not frequent"}, {"ko": "중심부", "en": "center; downtown area", "note": "The central or core region of a place"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ 것은 ~ㄴ 일이다", "exp": "Nominalized structure expressing evaluation of a fact: ''[thing] is a [type of] situation/event''.", "example_in_sentence": "이런 공격이 모스크바 중심부 근처에서 일어난 것은 흔하지 않은 일이에요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "국제 사회도 이 상황을 주의 깊게 지켜보고 있어요.", "translation": "The international community is also closely monitoring this situation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "국제 사회", "en": "international community", "note": "The collective term for countries and global stakeholders"}, {"ko": "지켜보다", "en": "to watch; to monitor; to observe", "note": "Implies attentive observation over time, often of developing situations"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect indicating an ongoing action.", "example_in_sentence": "주의 깊게 지켜보고 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "한국 외교부는 아직 이 사건에 대한 공식 입장을 발표하지 않았어요.", "translation": "South Korea''s Ministry of Foreign Affairs has not yet issued an official statement regarding this incident.", "vocab": [{"ko": "외교부", "en": "Ministry of Foreign Affairs", "note": "Government department handling international relations"}, {"ko": "입장", "en": "stance; position; statement", "note": "An official opinion or public stance on an issue"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~지 않다", "exp": "Negative form; indicates something has not happened or is not true.", "example_in_sentence": "공식 입장을 발표하지 않았어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "하지만 국제 정세 변화를 계속 관찰하고 있다고 해요.", "translation": "However, it is said that they continue to observe changes in the international situation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정세", "en": "situation; circumstances; state of affairs", "note": "Used for complex, developing political or social conditions"}, {"ko": "관찰하다", "en": "to observe; to monitor", "note": "More formal/technical than 지켜보다; implies systematic observation"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~다고 하다", "exp": "Indirect quotation or reported speech: ''it is said that; they say that''.", "example_in_sentence": "계속 관찰하고 있다고 해요"}], "analysis": []}]}', vocab = '[{"ko": "수도", "en": "capital (city)", "note": "Used with place names to indicate the main city of a country"}, {"ko": "드론", "en": "drone", "note": "Loanword; also called 무인기 (unmanned aircraft)"}, {"ko": "공격을 받다", "en": "to be attacked", "note": "Passive construction: literally ''receive an attack''"}, {"ko": "떨어지다", "en": "to be (located) away; to be distant", "note": "Past participle form of 떨어지다; modifies the noun 곳"}, {"ko": "킬로미터", "en": "kilometer", "note": "Loanword for metric distance unit"}, {"ko": "크렘린궁", "en": "the Kremlin", "note": "Proper noun; Russian presidential complex"}, {"ko": "대통령", "en": "president", "note": "Head of state in a country"}, {"ko": "민감하다", "en": "to be sensitive; to be delicate", "note": "Adjective describing topics that require caution"}, {"ko": "사안", "en": "matter; issue; case", "note": "Formal noun for a specific situation or problem"}, {"ko": "당국", "en": "authorities", "note": "Official government bodies or officials"}, {"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; case; event", "note": "Used for significant events, accidents, or crimes"}, {"ko": "흔하다", "en": "to be common (흔하지 않다 = uncommon)", "note": "Negated form of 흔하다; indicates something is not frequent"}, {"ko": "중심부", "en": "center; downtown area", "note": "The central or core region of a place"}, {"ko": "국제 사회", "en": "international community", "note": "The collective term for countries and global stakeholders"}, {"ko": "지켜보다", "en": "to watch; to monitor; to observe", "note": "Implies attentive observation over time, often of developing situations"}, {"ko": "외교부", "en": "Ministry of Foreign Affairs", "note": "Government department handling international relations"}, {"ko": "입장", "en": "stance; position; statement", "note": "An official opinion or public stance on an issue"}, {"ko": "정세", "en": "situation; circumstances; state of affairs", "note": "Used for complex, developing political or social conditions"}, {"ko": "관찰하다", "en": "to observe; to monitor", "note": "More formal/technical than 지켜보다; implies systematic observation"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mor76qdti4mh' and md5(translation) = 'fa0fb74d4e3eb02137e34e5f23ef5101';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A protest was held in Japan to protect the peace constitution. This protest was the largest scale so far.", "Prime Minister Takaichi is trying to change the constitution. Many Japanese citizens are opposing this.", "Japan''s peace constitution is a law that promises not to engage in war. This constitution was created after World War II.", "South Korea is also paying attention to Japan''s constitutional issues. Changes to Japan''s constitution could affect peace in East Asia."], "sentences": [{"text": "일본에서 평화 헌법을 지키자는 시위가 열렸어요.", "translation": "In Japan, a protest was held calling for the peace constitution to be protected.", "vocab": [{"ko": "평화", "en": "peace"}, {"ko": "헌법", "en": "constitution"}, {"ko": "지키다", "en": "to keep, protect"}, {"ko": "시위", "en": "protest, demonstration"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~자는 (quoted suggestion)", "exp": "Describes a noun with a ''let''s ~'' message. 지키다 → 지키자는 시위 = a protest saying ''let''s protect it''.", "example_in_sentence": "지키자는 시위"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense marker indicating completed action. Attaches to 열리다 (열렸어요) to show the protest already happened.", "example_in_sentence": "열렸어요"}]}, {"text": "이번 시위는 지금까지 중에서 가장 큰 규모였어요.", "translation": "This protest was the largest so far.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이번", "en": "this time"}, {"ko": "지금까지", "en": "so far, up to now"}, {"ko": "규모", "en": "scale, size"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 중에서", "exp": "Preposition-like expression meaning ''among'' or ''within''. Marks the scope of comparison.", "example_in_sentence": "지금까지 중에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "가장", "exp": "Superlative adverb meaning ''most'' or ''the largest''. Modifies the adjective 크다.", "example_in_sentence": "가장 큰"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이었어요/였어요 (past of 이다)", "exp": "Past tense of 이다 ''to be''. After a vowel it is 였어요: 규모 → 규모였어요 = was the scale.", "example_in_sentence": "규모였어요"}]}, {"text": "다카이치 총리가 헌법을 바꾸려고 하고 있어요.", "translation": "Prime Minister Takaichi is trying to change the constitution.", "vocab": [{"ko": "총리", "en": "prime minister"}, {"ko": "헌법", "en": "constitution"}, {"ko": "바꾸다", "en": "to change"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)려고", "exp": "Intention/purpose marker. Indicates the subject''s intention or plan. Connects verb stem 바꾸 to show the attempt.", "example_in_sentence": "바꾸려고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker. Shows ongoing action or state. 하다 + 고 있어요 indicates continuous activity.", "example_in_sentence": "하고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "많은 일본 국민들이 이것을 반대하고 있어요.", "translation": "Many Japanese citizens are opposing it.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많다", "en": "many, much"}, {"ko": "국민", "en": "citizen, people"}, {"ko": "반대하다", "en": "to oppose"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect. Shows the ongoing state of opposition. Attaches to 반대하다.", "example_in_sentence": "반대하고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "일본의 평화 헌법은 전쟁을 하지 않겠다고 약속한 법이에요.", "translation": "Japan''s peace constitution is a law that promises not to wage war.", "vocab": [{"ko": "평화", "en": "peace"}, {"ko": "전쟁", "en": "war"}, {"ko": "약속하다", "en": "to promise"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "Negative form. Expresses negation. Attaches to verb stem 하 to mean ''not do''.", "example_in_sentence": "하지 않겠다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~겠다", "exp": "Future intention or promise marker. Indicates future resolution. Combines with negation to express commitment not to act.", "example_in_sentence": "않겠다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 (indirect quotation)", "exp": "Reports what was said or promised. 하지 않겠다 → 하지 않겠다고 약속하다 = to promise not to do (it).", "example_in_sentence": "하지 않겠다고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past modifier)", "exp": "Past modifier for verbs. 약속하다 → 약속한 법 = a law that promised.", "example_in_sentence": "약속한 법"}]}, {"text": "이 헌법은 제2차 세계 대전 후에 만들어졌어요.", "translation": "This constitution was made after World War II.", "vocab": [{"ko": "헌법", "en": "constitution"}, {"ko": "세계 대전", "en": "world war"}, {"ko": "만들어지다", "en": "to be made"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어지다 (passive)", "exp": "Makes a verb passive. 만들다 → 만들어지다 ''to be made'' → 만들어졌어요 = was made.", "example_in_sentence": "만들어졌어요"}]}, {"text": "한국도 일본의 헌법 문제에 관심을 가지고 있어요.", "translation": "Korea is also paying attention to Japan''s constitutional issue.", "vocab": [{"ko": "헌법", "en": "constitution"}, {"ko": "문제", "en": "issue, problem"}, {"ko": "관심", "en": "interest, concern"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "관심을 가지다", "exp": "Idiomatic expression meaning ''to take interest'' or ''to pay attention''. Combines noun 관심 + verb 가지다.", "example_in_sentence": "관심을 가지고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect. Shows ongoing state of maintaining interest.", "example_in_sentence": "가지고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "일본의 헌법 변화는 동아시아 평화에 영향을 줄 수 있어요.", "translation": "Changes in Japan''s constitution can affect peace in East Asia.", "vocab": [{"ko": "헌법", "en": "constitution"}, {"ko": "변화", "en": "change"}, {"ko": "동아시아", "en": "East Asia"}, {"ko": "영향", "en": "influence, effect"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "영향을 주다", "exp": "Idiomatic expression meaning ''to have an impact on'' or ''to affect''. Combines noun 영향 + verb 주다.", "example_in_sentence": "영향을 줄"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Possibility or ability marker. Indicates potential/capacity. 주다→ 줄 수 있다 means ''can give/have an effect''.", "example_in_sentence": "줄 수 있어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "평화", "en": "peace", "note": ""}, {"ko": "헌법", "en": "constitution", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지키다", "en": "to keep, protect", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시위", "en": "protest, demonstration", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이번", "en": "this time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지금까지", "en": "so far, up to now", "note": ""}, {"ko": "규모", "en": "scale, size", "note": ""}, {"ko": "총리", "en": "prime minister", "note": ""}, {"ko": "바꾸다", "en": "to change", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "many, much", "note": ""}, {"ko": "국민", "en": "citizen, people", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반대하다", "en": "to oppose", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전쟁", "en": "war", "note": ""}, {"ko": "약속하다", "en": "to promise", "note": ""}, {"ko": "세계 대전", "en": "world war", "note": ""}, {"ko": "만들어지다", "en": "to be made", "note": ""}, {"ko": "문제", "en": "issue, problem", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관심", "en": "interest, concern", "note": ""}, {"ko": "변화", "en": "change", "note": ""}, {"ko": "동아시아", "en": "East Asia", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영향", "en": "influence, effect", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~자는 (quoted suggestion)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Describes a noun with a ''let''s ~'' message. 지키다 → 지키자는 시위 = a protest saying ''let''s protect it''.", "ex_ko": "일본에서 평화 헌법을 지키자는 시위가 열렸어요.", "ex_en": "In Japan, a protest was held calling for the peace constitution to be protected."}, {"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense marker indicating completed action. Attaches to 열리다 (열렸어요) to show the protest already happened.", "ex_ko": "일본에서 평화 헌법을 지키자는 시위가 열렸어요.", "ex_en": "In Japan, a protest was held calling for the peace constitution to be protected."}, {"name": "가장", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Superlative adverb meaning ''most'' or ''the largest''. Modifies the adjective 크다.", "ex_ko": "이번 시위는 지금까지 중에서 가장 큰 규모였어요.", "ex_en": "This protest was the largest so far."}, {"name": "~이었어요/였어요 (past of 이다)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense of 이다 ''to be''. After a vowel it is 였어요: 규모 → 규모였어요 = was the scale.", "ex_ko": "이번 시위는 지금까지 중에서 가장 큰 규모였어요.", "ex_en": "This protest was the largest so far."}, {"name": "~(으)려고", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Intention/purpose marker. Indicates the subject''s intention or plan. Connects verb stem 바꾸 to show the attempt.", "ex_ko": "다카이치 총리가 헌법을 바꾸려고 하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Prime Minister Takaichi is trying to change the constitution."}, {"name": "~고 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker. Shows ongoing action or state. 하다 + 고 있어요 indicates continuous activity.", "ex_ko": "다카이치 총리가 헌법을 바꾸려고 하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Prime Minister Takaichi is trying to change the constitution."}, {"name": "~지 않다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Negative form. Expresses negation. Attaches to verb stem 하 to mean ''not do''.", "ex_ko": "일본의 평화 헌법은 전쟁을 하지 않겠다고 약속한 법이에요.", "ex_en": "Japan''s peace constitution is a law that promises not to wage war."}, {"name": "~겠다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Future intention or promise marker. Indicates future resolution. Combines with negation to express commitment not to act.", "ex_ko": "일본의 평화 헌법은 전쟁을 하지 않겠다고 약속한 법이에요.", "ex_en": "Japan''s peace constitution is a law that promises not to wage war."}, {"name": "~다고 (indirect quotation)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Reports what was said or promised. 하지 않겠다 → 하지 않겠다고 약속하다 = to promise not to do (it).", "ex_ko": "일본의 평화 헌법은 전쟁을 하지 않겠다고 약속한 법이에요.", "ex_en": "Japan''s peace constitution is a law that promises not to wage war."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past modifier for verbs. 약속하다 → 약속한 법 = a law that promised.", "ex_ko": "일본의 평화 헌법은 전쟁을 하지 않겠다고 약속한 법이에요.", "ex_en": "Japan''s peace constitution is a law that promises not to wage war."}, {"name": "~아/어지다 (passive)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Makes a verb passive. 만들다 → 만들어지다 ''to be made'' → 만들어졌어요 = was made.", "ex_ko": "이 헌법은 제2차 세계 대전 후에 만들어졌어요.", "ex_en": "This constitution was made after World War II."}, {"name": "~ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Possibility or ability marker. Indicates potential/capacity. 주다→ 줄 수 있다 means ''can give/have an effect''.", "ex_ko": "일본의 헌법 변화는 동아시아 평화에 영향을 줄 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "Changes in Japan''s constitution can affect peace in East Asia."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mor77lzkiw78' and md5(translation) = '69d93a82209b9fbabfdef02386c0d60d';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In one building in Bakersfield, California, 23 fires broke out over the course of a year. This building is an old building with historical value.", "This kind of thing is not happening only in this building. Other historical buildings in the Bakersfield area are also burning one by one. Experts say that this might not be a coincidence.", "Local residents are very worried about this situation. The fire department (the place that puts out fires) is investigating the cause of the fire. The police also joined the investigation.", "When historical buildings disappear, the culture and history of that area also vanish along with them. In Korea too, protecting old buildings is an important issue. It is a situation that requires measures to prevent fires like these."], "sentences": [{"text": "미국 캘리포니아주 베이커즈필드의 한 건물에서 1년 동안 23번의 화재가 발생했어요.", "translation": "In one building in Bakersfield, California, 23 fires broke out over the course of a year.", "vocab": [{"ko": "건물", "en": "building", "note": ""}, {"ko": "화재", "en": "fire (incident)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발생하다", "en": "to occur, break out", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 동안", "exp": "\"during / for (a period)\". 1년 → 1년 동안 = \"for a year / over a year\".", "example_in_sentence": "1년 동안"}]}, {"text": "이 건물은 역사적 가치가 있는 오래된 건물이에요.", "translation": "This building is an old building with historical value.", "vocab": [{"ko": "역사적", "en": "historical", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가치", "en": "value", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오래되다", "en": "to be old (of objects)", "note": "oft. attributive 오래된"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~적 (-ic / -al adjective suffix)", "exp": "Sino-Korean noun → adjective. 역사 → 역사적 = \"historical\".", "example_in_sentence": "역사적 가치"}]}, {"text": "이런 일이 이 건물에서만 일어나는 것이 아니에요.", "translation": "This kind of thing is not happening only in this building.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen, occur", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것이 아니다", "exp": "Means ''it is not that ~''. 일어나다 → 일어나는 것이 아니에요 = it is not (only) happening.", "example_in_sentence": "일어나는 것이 아니에요"}]}, {"text": "베이커즈필드 지역의 다른 역사적인 건물들도 하나씩 불타고 있어요.", "translation": "Other historical buildings in the Bakersfield area are also burning one by one.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지역", "en": "area, region", "note": ""}, {"ko": "불타다", "en": "to burn (catch fire)", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (continuous)", "exp": "progressive aspect. 불타다 → 불타고 있다 = \"is burning\".", "example_in_sentence": "불타고 있어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~적 (-ic / -al adjective suffix)", "exp": "역사 → 역사적인 = \"historical (modifier form)\".", "example_in_sentence": "역사적인 건물들"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~씩 (each / per)", "exp": "distributive. 하나 → 하나씩 = \"one by one / one each\".", "example_in_sentence": "하나씩"}]}, {"text": "전문가들은 이것이 우연이 아닐 수도 있다고 말해요.", "translation": "Experts say that this might not be a coincidence.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert", "note": ""}, {"ko": "우연", "en": "coincidence, chance", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 말하다", "exp": "Reports what someone says. 있다 → 있다고 말해요 = (they) say that it may be.", "example_in_sentence": "있다고 말해요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수도 있다", "exp": "\"might / may possibly\". 아니다 → 아닐 수도 있다 = \"might not be\".", "example_in_sentence": "아닐 수도 있다"}]}, {"text": "지역 주민들은 이 상황을 매우 걱정하고 있어요.", "translation": "Local residents are very worried about this situation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "주민", "en": "resident", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "걱정하다", "en": "to worry", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (continuous)", "exp": "progressive aspect. 걱정하다 → 걱정하고 있다 = \"is worrying / is worried\".", "example_in_sentence": "걱정하고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "소방서(불을 끄는 일을 하는 곳)는 화재 원인을 조사하고 있어요.", "translation": "The fire department (the place that puts out fires) is investigating the cause of the fire.", "vocab": [{"ko": "소방서", "en": "fire station", "note": ""}, {"ko": "끄다", "en": "to put out, turn off", "note": "으-irregular: 끄+어 → 꺼"}, {"ko": "원인", "en": "cause", "note": ""}, {"ko": "조사하다", "en": "to investigate", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (continuous)", "exp": "progressive aspect. 조사하다 → 조사하고 있다 = \"is investigating\".", "example_in_sentence": "조사하고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "경찰도 함께 수사에 나섰어요.", "translation": "The police also joined the investigation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "경찰", "en": "police", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수사", "en": "investigation (criminal)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나서다", "en": "to step forward, take part", "note": ""}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "역사적인 건물들이 사라지면 그 지역의 문화와 역사도 함께 없어져요.", "translation": "When historical buildings disappear, the culture and history of that area also vanish along with them.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사라지다", "en": "to disappear", "note": ""}, {"ko": "문화", "en": "culture", "note": ""}, {"ko": "없어지다", "en": "to vanish, be gone", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (if/when)", "exp": "conditional. 사라지다 → 사라지면 = \"if / when (they) disappear\".", "example_in_sentence": "사라지면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~적 (-ic / -al adjective suffix)", "exp": "역사 → 역사적인 = \"historical\". Modifier form 적인 N.", "example_in_sentence": "역사적인 건물들"}]}, {"text": "한국에서도 오래된 건물을 보호하는 것이 중요한 문제예요.", "translation": "In Korea too, protecting old buildings is an important issue.", "vocab": [{"ko": "보호하다", "en": "to protect", "note": ""}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": ""}, {"ko": "문제", "en": "problem, issue", "note": ""}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이런 화재를 막기 위한 대책이 필요한 상황이에요.", "translation": "It is a situation that requires measures to prevent fires like these.", "vocab": [{"ko": "막다", "en": "to block, prevent", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대책", "en": "countermeasure, plan", "note": ""}, {"ko": "필요하다", "en": "to be necessary", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~기 위한 / ~기 위해", "exp": "purpose: \"in order to / for the sake of\". 막다 → 막기 위한 대책 = \"measures (intended) to prevent\".", "example_in_sentence": "막기 위한"}]}], "version": "s5"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "건물", "en": "building", "note": ""}, {"ko": "화재", "en": "fire (incident)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발생하다", "en": "to occur, break out", "note": ""}, {"ko": "역사적", "en": "historical", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가치", "en": "value", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오래되다", "en": "to be old (of objects)", "note": "oft. attributive 오래된"}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen, occur", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지역", "en": "area, region", "note": ""}, {"ko": "불타다", "en": "to burn (catch fire)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert", "note": ""}, {"ko": "우연", "en": "coincidence, chance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주민", "en": "resident", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "걱정하다", "en": "to worry", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소방서", "en": "fire station", "note": ""}, {"ko": "끄다", "en": "to put out, turn off", "note": "으-irregular: 끄+어 → 꺼"}, {"ko": "원인", "en": "cause", "note": ""}, {"ko": "조사하다", "en": "to investigate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "경찰", "en": "police", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수사", "en": "investigation (criminal)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나서다", "en": "to step forward, take part", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사라지다", "en": "to disappear", "note": ""}, {"ko": "문화", "en": "culture", "note": ""}, {"ko": "없어지다", "en": "to vanish, be gone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보호하다", "en": "to protect", "note": ""}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": ""}, {"ko": "문제", "en": "problem, issue", "note": ""}, {"ko": "막다", "en": "to block, prevent", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대책", "en": "countermeasure, plan", "note": ""}, {"ko": "필요하다", "en": "to be necessary", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~적 (-ic / -al adjective suffix)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Sino-Korean noun → adjective. 역사 → 역사적 = \"historical\".", "ex_ko": "이 건물은 역사적 가치가 있는 오래된 건물이에요.", "ex_en": "This building is an old building with historical value."}, {"name": "~는 것이 아니다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''it is not that ~''. 일어나다 → 일어나는 것이 아니에요 = it is not (only) happening.", "ex_ko": "이런 일이 이 건물에서만 일어나는 것이 아니에요.", "ex_en": "This kind of thing is not happening only in this building."}, {"name": "~고 있다 (continuous)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "progressive aspect. 걱정하다 → 걱정하고 있다 = \"is worrying / is worried\".", "ex_ko": "베이커즈필드 지역의 다른 역사적인 건물들도 하나씩 불타고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Other historical buildings in the Bakersfield area are also burning one by one."}, {"name": "~씩 (each / per)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "distributive. 하나 → 하나씩 = \"one by one / one each\".", "ex_ko": "베이커즈필드 지역의 다른 역사적인 건물들도 하나씩 불타고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Other historical buildings in the Bakersfield area are also burning one by one."}, {"name": "~다고 말하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reports what someone says. 있다 → 있다고 말해요 = (they) say that it may be.", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 이것이 우연이 아닐 수도 있다고 말해요.", "ex_en": "Experts say that this might not be a coincidence."}, {"name": "~(으)면 (if/when)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "conditional. 사라지다 → 사라지면 = \"if / when (they) disappear\".", "ex_ko": "역사적인 건물들이 사라지면 그 지역의 문화와 역사도 함께 없어져요.", "ex_en": "When historical buildings disappear, the culture and history of that area also vanish along with them."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mortm5de1mh0' and md5(translation) = '84202e584660da7e6631ed9b51604d92';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "타이완 반도체 제조회사(TSMC)에 대한 산업스파이 활동으로 기소된 범죄자들이 최대 10년의 징역형을 선고받았어요.", "idx": 0, "translation": "Criminals indicted for industrial espionage against Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company (TSMC) were sentenced to up to 10 years imprisonment.", "vocab": [{"ko": "반도체", "en": "semiconductor", "note": "core component in modern electronics"}, {"ko": "산업스파이", "en": "industrial espionage", "note": "stealing corporate/industrial secrets"}, {"ko": "기소하다", "en": "to indict; to prosecute", "note": "legal term"}, {"ko": "징역형", "en": "prison sentence", "note": "imprisonment as punishment"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~에 대한", "exp": "expresses ''against'' or ''regarding''; shows the target of an action", "example_in_sentence": "타이완 반도체 제조회사(TSMC)에 대한 산업스파이 활동"}, {"pattern": "~으로 기소되다", "exp": "passive construction meaning ''to be indicted/prosecuted for''", "example_in_sentence": "산업스파이 활동으로 기소된"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 사건은 반도체 기술 유출과 관련된 중대한 경제범죄로 분류되었습니다.", "idx": 1, "translation": "This case was classified as a serious economic crime related to semiconductor technology leakage.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기술 유출", "en": "technology leakage; technology theft", "note": "unauthorized disclosure of technical information"}, {"ko": "경제범죄", "en": "economic crime", "note": "crime involving financial/economic damage"}, {"ko": "중대하다", "en": "serious; grave; critical", "note": "adjective form"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~과 관련된", "exp": "relational modifier meaning ''related to''; ''connected with''", "example_in_sentence": "반도체 기술 유출과 관련된 중대한 경제범죄"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "반도체는 현대 기술의 핵심 부품으로, 스마트폰부터 자동차까지 모든 전자제품에 사용돼요.", "idx": 2, "translation": "Semiconductors are a core component of modern technology, used in all electronic products from smartphones to automobiles.", "vocab": [{"ko": "핵심 부품", "en": "core component; essential part", "note": "key/vital component"}, {"ko": "스마트폰", "en": "smartphone", "note": "from English"}, {"ko": "전자제품", "en": "electronic product", "note": "appliance; device"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~부터 ~까지", "exp": "expresses range from X to Y, inclusive of both endpoints", "example_in_sentence": "스마트폰부터 자동차까지"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "특히 타이완은 전 세계 반도체 생산의 60% 이상을 담당하는 핵심 국가입니다.", "idx": 3, "translation": "In particular, Taiwan is a core country that handles over 60% of global semiconductor production.", "vocab": [{"ko": "담당하다", "en": "to be responsible for; to handle; to manage", "note": "verb"}, {"ko": "전 세계", "en": "the entire world; globally", "note": "noun"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~이상", "exp": "means ''over; more than; or more''; indicates a minimum threshold", "example_in_sentence": "60% 이상을"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "따라서 이런 기술 정보는 국가 기밀에 준하는 중요성을 갖고 있어요.", "idx": 4, "translation": "Therefore, such technical information holds importance equivalent to national secrets.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기술 정보", "en": "technical information", "note": "information about technology"}, {"ko": "국가 기밀", "en": "national secret; state secret", "note": "confidential government information"}, {"ko": "중요성", "en": "importance; significance", "note": "abstract noun"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~에 준하다", "exp": "means ''to be equivalent to; to match in level/importance''", "example_in_sentence": "국가 기밀에 준하는 중요성"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이번 판결은 산업스파이 활동에 대한 강력한 경고 메시지를 담고 있습니다.", "idx": 5, "translation": "This ruling contains a strong warning message against industrial espionage activities.", "vocab": [{"ko": "판결", "en": "judicial ruling; verdict; decision", "note": "from a court"}, {"ko": "경고 메시지", "en": "warning message", "note": "cautionary statement"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~을/를 담다", "exp": "verb meaning ''to contain; to embody; to hold''; metaphorical sense of ''include/express''", "example_in_sentence": "강력한 경고 메시지를 담고 있습니다"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "법원은 기업 기밀 유출이 단순한 개인 범죄가 아니라 국가 경제 안보를 위협하는 중대 범죄라고 판단했어요.", "idx": 6, "translation": "The court determined that leaking corporate secrets is not a simple individual crime but a serious crime that threatens national economic security.", "vocab": [{"ko": "법원", "en": "court", "note": "judicial institution"}, {"ko": "기업 기밀", "en": "corporate secret; trade secret", "note": "company confidential information"}, {"ko": "경제 안보", "en": "economic security", "note": "protection of economic interests"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~이 아니라 ~", "exp": "negation pattern meaning ''not X but rather Y''; contrasts two things", "example_in_sentence": "단순한 개인 범죄가 아니라 국가 경제 안보를 위협하는 중대 범죄"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "한국도 반도체 강국으로서 비슷한 위험에 노출되어 있습니다.", "idx": 7, "translation": "Korea, as a semiconductor powerhouse, is also exposed to similar risks.", "vocab": [{"ko": "강국", "en": "powerhouse; major power; strong nation", "note": "powerful country/industry"}, {"ko": "위험", "en": "risk; danger; hazard", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "노출되다", "en": "to be exposed to", "note": "passive verb"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~로서", "exp": "particle meaning ''as; in one''s capacity as''; marks role or position", "example_in_sentence": "반도체 강국으로서"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "삼성전자와 에스케이하이닉스 같은 국내 반도체 기업들도 기술 보안에 더욱 신경 써야 할 것으로 보여요.", "idx": 8, "translation": "It seems that domestic semiconductor companies such as Samsung Electronics and SK Hynix will also need to pay more attention to technology security.", "vocab": [{"ko": "국내", "en": "domestic; internal; in-country", "note": "within the country"}, {"ko": "기술 보안", "en": "technology security", "note": "protecting technical information"}, {"ko": "신경 쓰다", "en": "to pay attention; to be concerned; to care", "note": "colloquial expression"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄹ 것으로 보이다", "exp": "prospective form meaning ''appears to; seems likely to; is expected to''", "example_in_sentence": "더욱 신경 써야 할 것으로 보여요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이번 사건을 통해 각국이 첨단 기술 보호에 얼마나 민감한지 알 수 있습니다.", "idx": 9, "translation": "Through this case, one can see how sensitive each country is to the protection of advanced technology.", "vocab": [{"ko": "첨단 기술", "en": "advanced technology; cutting-edge technology", "note": "high-tech; sophisticated"}, {"ko": "민감하다", "en": "sensitive; touchy; responsive", "note": "adjective"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~을/를 통해", "exp": "means ''through; via; by means of''; indicates a method or medium", "example_in_sentence": "이번 사건을 통해"}], "analysis": []}], "version": "p3"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "반도체", "en": "semiconductor", "note": "core component in modern electronics"}, {"ko": "산업스파이", "en": "industrial espionage", "note": "stealing corporate/industrial secrets"}, {"ko": "기소하다", "en": "to indict; to prosecute", "note": "legal term"}, {"ko": "징역형", "en": "prison sentence", "note": "imprisonment as punishment"}, {"ko": "기술 유출", "en": "technology leakage; technology theft", "note": "unauthorized disclosure of technical information"}, {"ko": "경제범죄", "en": "economic crime", "note": "crime involving financial/economic damage"}, {"ko": "중대하다", "en": "serious; grave; critical", "note": "adjective form"}, {"ko": "핵심 부품", "en": "core component; essential part", "note": "key/vital component"}, {"ko": "스마트폰", "en": "smartphone", "note": "from English"}, {"ko": "전자제품", "en": "electronic product", "note": "appliance; device"}, {"ko": "담당하다", "en": "to be responsible for; to handle; to manage", "note": "verb"}, {"ko": "전 세계", "en": "the entire world; globally", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "기술 정보", "en": "technical information", "note": "information about technology"}, {"ko": "국가 기밀", "en": "national secret; state secret", "note": "confidential government information"}, {"ko": "중요성", "en": "importance; significance", "note": "abstract noun"}, {"ko": "판결", "en": "judicial ruling; verdict; decision", "note": "from a court"}, {"ko": "경고 메시지", "en": "warning message", "note": "cautionary statement"}, {"ko": "법원", "en": "court", "note": "judicial institution"}, {"ko": "기업 기밀", "en": "corporate secret; trade secret", "note": "company confidential information"}, {"ko": "경제 안보", "en": "economic security", "note": "protection of economic interests"}, {"ko": "강국", "en": "powerhouse; major power; strong nation", "note": "powerful country/industry"}, {"ko": "위험", "en": "risk; danger; hazard", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "노출되다", "en": "to be exposed to", "note": "passive verb"}, {"ko": "국내", "en": "domestic; internal; in-country", "note": "within the country"}, {"ko": "기술 보안", "en": "technology security", "note": "protecting technical information"}, {"ko": "신경 쓰다", "en": "to pay attention; to be concerned; to care", "note": "colloquial expression"}, {"ko": "첨단 기술", "en": "advanced technology; cutting-edge technology", "note": "high-tech; sophisticated"}, {"ko": "민감하다", "en": "sensitive; touchy; responsive", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "선고받다", "en": "to be sentenced", "note": "Passive; compound of 선고 (sentencing) + 받다 (to receive)"}, {"ko": "분류하다", "en": "to classify; to categorize", "note": "Takes ~으로 for the category; in passive voice 분류되었다"}, {"ko": "유출", "en": "leakage; disclosure", "note": "Formal noun; 유출되다 (to leak); used for information/secrets escape"}, {"ko": "사용되다", "en": "to be used", "note": "Passive voice of 사용하다; combines with ~도록 or stands alone with ~ㄴ/~어"}, {"ko": "핵심 국가", "en": "key country", "note": "핵심 (core/critical) + 국가 (country); formal political/economic register"}, {"ko": "준하다", "en": "to be comparable to; to be equivalent to", "note": "Takes ~에; marks a level of equivalence or similarity without identity; 준하는 as relative clause"}, {"ko": "위협하다", "en": "to threaten", "note": "Takes object with ~을/를; 위협하는 as relative clause modifier"}, {"ko": "보안", "en": "security", "note": "보 (protection) + 안 (safety); modern formal term; 기술 보안 (technology security)"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mortmxn5ubv7' and md5(translation) = 'a6c14ee4c4a2b8b1aff950f7b783f738';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A 20-year-old young man living in Vietnam was on his way home after finishing training. At that moment, he discovered a house that was on fire.", "The young man climbed onto the roof together with other people. And he rescued two elderly people who were inside the house first.", "However, there were more family members still trapped inside the house. Two women and three children were unable to get out of the fire.", "The young man went back into the burning house again. And he safely rescued all five family members. Many people are praising this brave young man."], "sentences": [{"text": "베트남에 사는 20살 청년이 훈련을 마치고 집으로 돌아가는 길이었어요.", "translation": "A 20-year-old young man living in Vietnam was on his way home after finishing training.", "vocab": [{"ko": "베트남", "en": "Vietnam", "note": "country name; used with ~에 살다 (live in)"}, {"ko": "훈련", "en": "training", "note": "noun; paired with 마치다 (finish)"}, {"ko": "마치다", "en": "to finish, complete", "note": "action completed before another; often followed by ~고"}, {"ko": "돌아가다", "en": "to return, go back", "note": "movement verb; direction marked with ~으로"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~는 중이다 / ~는 길이다", "exp": "Describes an action or state in progress at a specific moment; ~는 길이다 emphasizes being in the process of going/moving.", "example_in_sentence": "집으로 돌아가는 길이었어요"}, {"pattern": "~고 (sequential action)", "exp": "Connects two completed actions in order; the first action happens, then the second.", "example_in_sentence": "훈련을 마치고 집으로 돌아가는"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그때 한 집에서 불이 나고 있는 것을 발견했어요.", "translation": "At that moment, he discovered a house that was on fire.", "vocab": [{"ko": "불", "en": "fire", "note": "noun; 불이 나다 (fire breaks out)"}, {"ko": "나다", "en": "to break out, occur", "note": "used with 불 to mean ''fire starts''; different from other meanings of 나다"}, {"ko": "발견하다", "en": "to discover, find", "note": "transitive verb; takes object with ~을/를"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 있는 것", "exp": "Nominalization of an ongoing action; ''something that is happening''; ~는 것 focuses on the state/action itself.", "example_in_sentence": "불이 나고 있는 것을 발견했어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "청년은 다른 사람들과 함께 지붕으로 올라갔어요.", "translation": "The young man climbed onto the roof together with other people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "다른", "en": "other, different", "note": "adjective; modifies 사람들"}, {"ko": "함께", "en": "together", "note": "adverb; indicates joint action"}, {"ko": "지붕", "en": "roof", "note": "noun; location marked with ~으로"}, {"ko": "올라가다", "en": "to go up, climb", "note": "movement upward; direction marked with ~으로"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그리고 집 안에 있던 노인 두 명을 먼저 구했어요.", "translation": "And first, he rescued two elderly people who were inside the house.", "vocab": [{"ko": "노인", "en": "elderly person", "note": "noun; 두 명 (two people) is the count"}, {"ko": "먼저", "en": "first, beforehand", "note": "adverb; marks priority or sequence"}, {"ko": "구하다", "en": "to rescue, save", "note": "transitive verb; takes object with ~을/를"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~던 (past modifier)", "exp": "Describes a state or action that existed in the past; modifies the following noun.", "example_in_sentence": "집 안에 있던 노인"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "하지만 아직 집 안에 갇힌 가족이 더 있었어요.", "translation": "However, there were more family members still trapped inside the house.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "however, but", "note": "conjunction; introduces contrast"}, {"ko": "아직", "en": "still, yet", "note": "adverb; indicates continuation or remaining action"}, {"ko": "갇히다", "en": "to be trapped, confined", "note": "passive verb; ~ㄴ form modifies following noun"}, {"ko": "가족", "en": "family", "note": "noun; ~이 더 있었어요 (there were more)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ (past participle modifier)", "exp": "Modifies a noun to describe a completed or existing state; here marks a trapped condition.", "example_in_sentence": "갇힌 가족"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "여성 두 명과 아이 세 명이 불 속에서 나오지 못하고 있었어요.", "translation": "Two women and three children were unable to get out of the fire.", "vocab": [{"ko": "여성", "en": "woman, female", "note": "formal noun; paired with 아이 (child)"}, {"ko": "아이", "en": "child", "note": "noun; counted with 명"}, {"ko": "나오다", "en": "to come out, emerge", "note": "movement verb; negated with ~지 못하다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~지 못하다 (inability/failure)", "exp": "Expresses inability or failure to complete an action; ''cannot'' or ''was unable to''.", "example_in_sentence": "나오지 못하고 있었어요"}, {"pattern": "~고 있었어요 (past continuous)", "exp": "Describes an ongoing state or repeated action in the past; emphasizes duration.", "example_in_sentence": "나오지 못하고 있었어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "청년은 다시 불타는 집 안으로 들어갔어요.", "translation": "The young man went back into the burning house again.", "vocab": [{"ko": "다시", "en": "again, once more", "note": "adverb; marks repetition"}, {"ko": "불타다", "en": "to burn, be on fire", "note": "verb; ~는 form modifies following noun"}, {"ko": "들어가다", "en": "to enter, go in", "note": "movement verb; direction marked with ~으로"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~는 (present participle modifier)", "exp": "Modifies a noun to describe an ongoing or habitual action; here describes the house as actively burning.", "example_in_sentence": "불타는 집"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그리고 가족 다섯 명을 모두 안전하게 구해냈어요.", "translation": "And he safely rescued all five family members.", "vocab": [{"ko": "안전하다", "en": "to be safe (안전하게 = safely)", "note": "adverb form of 안전하다; modifies the rescue action"}, {"ko": "구해내다", "en": "to rescue, save (completely)", "note": "compound verb; ~어내다 emphasizes completing the action fully"}, {"ko": "모두", "en": "all, everyone", "note": "adverb; emphasizes totality"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 이 용감한 청년을 칭찬하고 있어요.", "translation": "Many people are praising this brave young man.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; to be a lot", "note": "adjective; modifies 사람들"}, {"ko": "용감하다", "en": "to be brave; to be courageous", "note": "adjective; modifies 청년"}, {"ko": "칭찬하다", "en": "to praise, compliment", "note": "transitive verb; takes object with ~을/를"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 있다 (present continuous)", "exp": "Describes an action ongoing in the present; emphasizes the continuous or repeated nature.", "example_in_sentence": "칭찬하고 있어요"}], "analysis": []}]}', vocab = '[{"ko": "베트남", "en": "Vietnam", "note": "country name; used with ~에 살다 (live in)"}, {"ko": "훈련", "en": "training", "note": "noun; paired with 마치다 (finish)"}, {"ko": "마치다", "en": "to finish, complete", "note": "action completed before another; often followed by ~고"}, {"ko": "돌아가다", "en": "to return, go back", "note": "movement verb; direction marked with ~으로"}, {"ko": "불", "en": "fire", "note": "noun; 불이 나다 (fire breaks out)"}, {"ko": "나다", "en": "to break out, occur", "note": "used with 불 to mean ''fire starts''; different from other meanings of 나다"}, {"ko": "발견하다", "en": "to discover, find", "note": "transitive verb; takes object with ~을/를"}, {"ko": "다른", "en": "other, different", "note": "adjective; modifies 사람들"}, {"ko": "함께", "en": "together", "note": "adverb; indicates joint action"}, {"ko": "지붕", "en": "roof", "note": "noun; location marked with ~으로"}, {"ko": "올라가다", "en": "to go up, climb", "note": "movement upward; direction marked with ~으로"}, {"ko": "노인", "en": "elderly person", "note": "noun; 두 명 (two people) is the count"}, {"ko": "먼저", "en": "first, beforehand", "note": "adverb; marks priority or sequence"}, {"ko": "구하다", "en": "to rescue, save", "note": "transitive verb; takes object with ~을/를"}, {"ko": "하지만", "en": "however, but", "note": "conjunction; introduces contrast"}, {"ko": "아직", "en": "still, yet", "note": "adverb; indicates continuation or remaining action"}, {"ko": "갇히다", "en": "to be trapped, confined", "note": "passive verb; ~ㄴ form modifies following noun"}, {"ko": "가족", "en": "family", "note": "noun; ~이 더 있었어요 (there were more)"}, {"ko": "여성", "en": "woman, female", "note": "formal noun; paired with 아이 (child)"}, {"ko": "아이", "en": "child", "note": "noun; counted with 명"}, {"ko": "나오다", "en": "to come out, emerge", "note": "movement verb; negated with ~지 못하다"}, {"ko": "다시", "en": "again, once more", "note": "adverb; marks repetition"}, {"ko": "불타다", "en": "to burn, be on fire", "note": "verb; ~는 form modifies following noun"}, {"ko": "들어가다", "en": "to enter, go in", "note": "movement verb; direction marked with ~으로"}, {"ko": "안전하다", "en": "to be safe (안전하게 = safely)", "note": "adverb form of 안전하다; modifies the rescue action"}, {"ko": "구해내다", "en": "to rescue, save (completely)", "note": "compound verb; ~어내다 emphasizes completing the action fully"}, {"ko": "모두", "en": "all, everyone", "note": "adverb; emphasizes totality"}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many; to be a lot", "note": "adjective; modifies 사람들"}, {"ko": "용감하다", "en": "to be brave; to be courageous", "note": "adjective; modifies 청년"}, {"ko": "칭찬하다", "en": "to praise, compliment", "note": "transitive verb; takes object with ~을/를"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mortntpdue4g' and md5(translation) = 'af4c3da3640696bc36de8f409e8597b9';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["There lives a special snail in the sea. Its name is the scale-foot snail.", "This snail is truly remarkable. It attaches iron to its body to survive. Other animals cannot attach iron to their bodies.", "The scale-foot snail''s shell is made of iron. It looks just like wearing armor (hard protective clothing) to protect the body. This armor protects the snail.", "Scientists are studying this snail diligently. They want to discover the secret of the iron armor."], "sentences": [{"text": "바다에 특별한 달팽이가 살아요.", "translation": "A special snail lives in the sea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "바다", "en": "sea", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "달팽이", "en": "snail", "note": ""}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이름은 비늘발 달팽이예요.", "translation": "Its name is the scale-foot snail.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이름", "en": "name", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비늘발", "en": "scale-foot", "note": "compound noun; 비늘 = scale, 발 = foot"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 달팽이는 정말 신기해요.", "translation": "This snail is truly remarkable.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정말", "en": "truly; really", "note": "adverb modifying adjectives"}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be remarkable; to be amazing", "note": ""}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "몸에 쇠를 붙여서 살아요.", "translation": "It attaches iron to its body to survive.", "vocab": [{"ko": "쇠", "en": "iron", "note": ""}, {"ko": "붙이다", "en": "to attach; to stick", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~어서", "exp": "Connective indicating purpose or reason; here expressing purpose (in order to).", "example_in_sentence": "붙여서 살아요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "다른 동물들은 쇠를 몸에 붙이지 못해요.", "translation": "Other animals cannot attach iron to their bodies.", "vocab": [{"ko": "다른", "en": "other; different", "note": ""}, {"ko": "동물", "en": "animal", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~지 못하다", "exp": "Negation expressing inability or failure to do something.", "example_in_sentence": "붙이지 못해요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "비늘발 달팽이의 껍질은 쇠로 만들어져요.", "translation": "The scale-foot snail''s shell is made of iron.", "vocab": [{"ko": "껍질", "en": "shell; skin", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~로 만들어지다", "exp": "Passive voice expressing that something is made or constructed from a material.", "example_in_sentence": "쇠로 만들어져요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "마치 갑옷(몸을 보호하는 단단한 옷)을 입은 것 같아요.", "translation": "It looks just like it is wearing armor (hard clothing that protects the body).", "vocab": [{"ko": "마치", "en": "just like; as if", "note": "adverb of comparison"}, {"ko": "갑옷", "en": "armor", "note": "hard protective clothing worn in battle"}, {"ko": "입다", "en": "to wear; to put on", "note": "for clothing"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ 것 같다", "exp": "Expresses appearance or conjecture; ''looks like'' or ''seems like''.", "example_in_sentence": "입은 것 같아요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 갑옷이 달팽이를 지켜 줘요.", "translation": "This armor protects the snail.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지키다", "en": "to protect; to guard", "note": ""}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "과학자들이 이 달팽이를 열심히 연구하고 있어요.", "translation": "Scientists are studying this snail diligently.", "vocab": [{"ko": "과학자", "en": "scientist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "열심히", "en": "diligently; earnestly", "note": "adverb modifying verbs"}, {"ko": "연구하다", "en": "to study; to research", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect; indicates an ongoing action in the present.", "example_in_sentence": "연구하고 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "쇠 갑옷의 비밀을 알고 싶어 해요.", "translation": "They want to discover the secret of the iron armor.", "vocab": [{"ko": "비밀", "en": "secret", "note": ""}, {"ko": "알다", "en": "to know; to discover", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 싶다", "exp": "Expresses desire or wish to do something.", "example_in_sentence": "알고 싶어 해요"}], "analysis": []}]}', vocab = '[{"ko": "바다", "en": "sea", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "달팽이", "en": "snail", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이름", "en": "name", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비늘발", "en": "scale-foot", "note": "compound noun; 비늘 = scale, 발 = foot"}, {"ko": "정말", "en": "truly; really", "note": "adverb modifying adjectives"}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be remarkable; to be amazing", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쇠", "en": "iron", "note": ""}, {"ko": "붙이다", "en": "to attach; to stick", "note": ""}, {"ko": "다른", "en": "other; different", "note": ""}, {"ko": "동물", "en": "animal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "껍질", "en": "shell; skin", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마치", "en": "just like; as if", "note": "adverb of comparison"}, {"ko": "갑옷", "en": "armor", "note": "hard protective clothing worn in battle"}, {"ko": "입다", "en": "to wear; to put on", "note": "for clothing"}, {"ko": "지키다", "en": "to protect; to guard", "note": ""}, {"ko": "과학자", "en": "scientist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "열심히", "en": "diligently; earnestly", "note": "adverb modifying verbs"}, {"ko": "연구하다", "en": "to study; to research", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비밀", "en": "secret", "note": ""}, {"ko": "알다", "en": "to know; to discover", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mortodw2ex33' and md5(translation) = '9167433f81742b5b2dd5fe85f905d0bc';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In 2014, a man named Igor Vorozhbichyn was attacked by a bear in Russia. When the bear attacked him, he was in a life-threatening situation where he could have died.", "However, his cell phone suddenly rang. The ringtone was the song \"Baby\" by Justin Bieber.", "The bear was startled by the sudden sound. And the bear became frightened and ran away. Thanks to this, the man was able to survive.", "This story became known as a remarkable incident to people around the world. Sometimes unexpected things can help us."], "sentences": [{"text": "2014년 러시아에서 이고르 보로즈비친이라는 남성이 곰에게 공격을 받았어요.", "translation": "In 2014, a man named Igor Vorozhbichyn was attacked by a bear in Russia.", "vocab": [{"ko": "러시아", "en": "Russia"}, {"ko": "남성", "en": "man"}, {"ko": "곰", "en": "bear"}, {"ko": "공격", "en": "attack"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라는", "exp": "Gives the name of the noun after it: ''called ~''. 이고르 보로즈비친이라는 남성 = a man called Igor Vorozhbichyn.", "example_in_sentence": "이고르 보로즈비친이라는 남성"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게", "exp": "Marks the agent/source in passive or indirect sentences. Indicates ''by'' or ''from'' a person.", "example_in_sentence": "곰에게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 받다", "exp": "Noun + 을/를 받다 means ''to receive / undergo ~''. 공격을 받다 = to be attacked.", "example_in_sentence": "공격을 받았어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense marker for completed action. From stem 받- + past suffix 았 + polite ending 어요.", "example_in_sentence": "받았어요"}]}, {"text": "곰이 그를 공격했을 때, 그는 죽을 수도 있는 위험한 상황이었어요.", "translation": "When the bear attacked him, he was in a dangerous situation in which he could possibly die.", "vocab": [{"ko": "공격하다", "en": "to attack"}, {"ko": "죽다", "en": "to die"}, {"ko": "위험하다", "en": "dangerous"}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었을 때", "exp": "Means ''when ~'' for a past event. 공격하다 → 공격했을 때 = when (it) attacked.", "example_in_sentence": "공격했을 때"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수도 있다", "exp": "Means ''might / could possibly''. 죽다 → 죽을 수도 있는 상황 = a situation where he could possibly die.", "example_in_sentence": "죽을 수도 있는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Lets an adjective describe a noun. 위험하다 → 위험한 상황 = a dangerous situation.", "example_in_sentence": "위험한 상황"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이었어요/였어요 (past of 이다)", "exp": "Past tense of 이다 ''to be''. After a consonant it is 이었어요: 상황 → 상황이었어요 = was a situation.", "example_in_sentence": "상황이었어요"}]}, {"text": "그런데 갑자기 그의 핸드폰이 울렸어요.", "translation": "But suddenly his phone rang.", "vocab": [{"ko": "갑자기", "en": "suddenly"}, {"ko": "핸드폰", "en": "phone"}, {"ko": "울리다", "en": "to ring"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "그런데", "exp": "Discourse connector meaning ''but'' or ''however''; introduces a contrasting or unexpected development.", "example_in_sentence": "그런데"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense marker for completed action. From stem 울리- + past suffix 었 + polite ending 어요.", "example_in_sentence": "울렸어요"}]}, {"text": "핸드폰 벨소리는 저스틴 비버(Justin Bieber)의 ''베이비(Baby)''라는 노래였어요.", "translation": "The phone ringtone was a song called ''Baby'' by Justin Bieber.", "vocab": [{"ko": "벨소리", "en": "ringtone"}, {"ko": "노래", "en": "song"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "Possessive particle, like ''s or ''of''. 저스틴 비버의 노래 = Justin Bieber''s song.", "example_in_sentence": "비버(Justin Bieber)의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라는", "exp": "Gives the name of the noun after it: ''called ~''. After a vowel it is 라는: ''베이비''라는 노래 = a song called ''Baby''.", "example_in_sentence": "''베이비(Baby)''라는 노래"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이었어요/였어요 (past of 이다)", "exp": "Past tense of 이다 ''to be''. After a vowel it is 였어요: 노래 → 노래였어요 = was a song.", "example_in_sentence": "노래였어요"}]}, {"text": "곰은 갑작스러운 소리에 깜짝 놀랐어요.", "translation": "The bear was startled by the sudden sound.", "vocab": [{"ko": "갑작스럽다", "en": "to be sudden"}, {"ko": "소리", "en": "sound"}, {"ko": "깜짝", "en": "with a start"}, {"ko": "놀라다", "en": "to be surprised/startled"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Lets an adjective describe a noun. 갑작스럽다 is ㅂ-irregular (ㅂ becomes 우): 갑작스럽다 → 갑작스러운 소리 = a sudden sound.", "example_in_sentence": "갑작스러운 소리"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "Locative or cause particle; marks the trigger or cause of an emotion/state.", "example_in_sentence": "소리에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense marker. From stem 놀라- + past suffix 았 + polite ending 어요.", "example_in_sentence": "놀랐어요"}]}, {"text": "그리고 곰은 무서워하며 도망갔어요.", "translation": "And the bear fled in fear.", "vocab": [{"ko": "무서워하다", "en": "to be/act afraid"}, {"ko": "도망가다", "en": "to flee/run away"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)며", "exp": "Written form of ~(으)면서: ''while / and''. 무서워하다 → 무서워하며 = while being scared.", "example_in_sentence": "무서워하며"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense marker. From stem 도망가- + past suffix 갔 + polite ending 어요.", "example_in_sentence": "도망갔어요"}]}, {"text": "이 덕분에 남성은 살 수 있었어요.", "translation": "Thanks to this, the man was able to survive.", "vocab": [{"ko": "덕분", "en": "thanks to"}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live/survive"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 덕분에", "exp": "Expression meaning ''thanks to'' or ''because of''; expresses gratitude or positive causality.", "example_in_sentence": "이 덕분에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Means ''can / be able to''. 살다 → 살 수 있었어요 = was able to survive.", "example_in_sentence": "살 수 있었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense marker. From 있- + past suffix 었 + polite ending 어요.", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}]}, {"text": "이 이야기는 전 세계 사람들에게 신기한 일로 알려졌어요.", "translation": "This story became known to people around the world as an amazing event.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이야기", "en": "story"}, {"ko": "전 세계", "en": "whole world"}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person"}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing; to be surprising"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게", "exp": "Marks the recipient or target in passive/receptive contexts. Indicates ''to'' a person.", "example_in_sentence": "사람들에게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Lets an adjective describe a noun. 신기하다 → 신기한 일 = an amazing event.", "example_in_sentence": "신기한 일"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (as)", "exp": "Particle meaning ''as'' (a role or category). After a vowel or ㄹ it is 로: 일 → 일로 = as an event.", "example_in_sentence": "일로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어지다 (passive)", "exp": "Makes a verb passive. 알리다 ''to let know'' → 알려지다 ''to become known'' → 알려졌어요 = became known.", "example_in_sentence": "알려졌어요"}]}, {"text": "때로는 예상하지 못한 것이 우리를 도와줄 수 있어요.", "translation": "Sometimes unexpected things can help us.", "vocab": [{"ko": "때로", "en": "sometimes"}, {"ko": "예상하다", "en": "to expect; to anticipate"}, {"ko": "도와주다", "en": "to help"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 못하다", "exp": "Negative auxiliary meaning ''unable to'' or ''fail to''. Negation marker 지 + 못 (unable) + 하다.", "example_in_sentence": "하지 못한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past modifier)", "exp": "Past modifier for verbs. 예상하지 못하다 → 예상하지 못한 것 = something (we) didn''t expect.", "example_in_sentence": "예상하지 못한 것"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Means ''can''. 도와주다 → 도와줄 수 있어요 = can help.", "example_in_sentence": "도와줄 수 있어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "러시아", "en": "Russia", "note": ""}, {"ko": "남성", "en": "man", "note": ""}, {"ko": "곰", "en": "bear", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공격", "en": "attack", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공격하다", "en": "to attack", "note": ""}, {"ko": "죽다", "en": "to die", "note": ""}, {"ko": "위험하다", "en": "dangerous", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "갑자기", "en": "suddenly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "핸드폰", "en": "phone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "울리다", "en": "to ring", "note": ""}, {"ko": "벨소리", "en": "ringtone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "노래", "en": "song", "note": ""}, {"ko": "갑작스럽다", "en": "to be sudden", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소리", "en": "sound", "note": ""}, {"ko": "깜짝", "en": "with a start", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀라다", "en": "to be surprised/startled", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무서워하다", "en": "to be/act afraid", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도망가다", "en": "to flee/run away", "note": ""}, {"ko": "덕분", "en": "thanks to", "note": ""}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live/survive", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이야기", "en": "story", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전 세계", "en": "whole world", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing; to be surprising", "note": ""}, {"ko": "때로", "en": "sometimes", "note": ""}, {"ko": "예상하다", "en": "to expect; to anticipate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도와주다", "en": "to help", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(이)라는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Gives the name of the noun after it: ''called ~''. After a vowel it is 라는: ''베이비''라는 노래 = a song called ''Baby''.", "ex_ko": "2014년 러시아에서 이고르 보로즈비친이라는 남성이 곰에게 공격을 받았어요.", "ex_en": "In 2014, a man named Igor Vorozhbichyn was attacked by a bear in Russia."}, {"name": "~에게", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks the agent/source in passive or indirect sentences. Indicates ''by'' or ''from'' a person.", "ex_ko": "2014년 러시아에서 이고르 보로즈비친이라는 남성이 곰에게 공격을 받았어요.", "ex_en": "In 2014, a man named Igor Vorozhbichyn was attacked by a bear in Russia."}, {"name": "~을/를 받다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Noun + 을/를 받다 means ''to receive / undergo ~''. 공격을 받다 = to be attacked.", "ex_ko": "2014년 러시아에서 이고르 보로즈비친이라는 남성이 곰에게 공격을 받았어요.", "ex_en": "In 2014, a man named Igor Vorozhbichyn was attacked by a bear in Russia."}, {"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense marker for completed action. From stem 울리- + past suffix 었 + polite ending 어요.", "ex_ko": "2014년 러시아에서 이고르 보로즈비친이라는 남성이 곰에게 공격을 받았어요.", "ex_en": "In 2014, a man named Igor Vorozhbichyn was attacked by a bear in Russia."}, {"name": "~았/었을 때", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''when ~'' for a past event. 공격하다 → 공격했을 때 = when (it) attacked.", "ex_ko": "곰이 그를 공격했을 때, 그는 죽을 수도 있는 위험한 상황이었어요.", "ex_en": "When the bear attacked him, he was in a dangerous situation in which he could possibly die."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수도 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''might / could possibly''. 죽다 → 죽을 수도 있는 상황 = a situation where he could possibly die.", "ex_ko": "곰이 그를 공격했을 때, 그는 죽을 수도 있는 위험한 상황이었어요.", "ex_en": "When the bear attacked him, he was in a dangerous situation in which he could possibly die."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Lets an adjective describe a noun. 갑작스럽다 is ㅂ-irregular (ㅂ becomes 우): 갑작스럽다 → 갑작스러운 소리 = a sudden sound.", "ex_ko": "곰이 그를 공격했을 때, 그는 죽을 수도 있는 위험한 상황이었어요.", "ex_en": "When the bear attacked him, he was in a dangerous situation in which he could possibly die."}, {"name": "~이었어요/였어요 (past of 이다)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense of 이다 ''to be''. After a consonant it is 이었어요: 상황 → 상황이었어요 = was a situation.", "ex_ko": "곰이 그를 공격했을 때, 그는 죽을 수도 있는 위험한 상황이었어요.", "ex_en": "When the bear attacked him, he was in a dangerous situation in which he could possibly die."}, {"name": "~의", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Possessive particle, like ''s or ''of''. 저스틴 비버의 노래 = Justin Bieber''s song.", "ex_ko": "핸드폰 벨소리는 저스틴 비버(Justin Bieber)의 ''베이비(Baby)''라는 노래였어요.", "ex_en": "The phone ringtone was a song called ''Baby'' by Justin Bieber."}, {"name": "~에", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Locative or cause particle; marks the trigger or cause of an emotion/state.", "ex_ko": "곰은 갑작스러운 소리에 깜짝 놀랐어요.", "ex_en": "The bear was startled by the sudden sound."}, {"name": "~(으)며", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Written form of ~(으)면서: ''while / and''. 무서워하다 → 무서워하며 = while being scared.", "ex_ko": "그리고 곰은 무서워하며 도망갔어요.", "ex_en": "And the bear fled in fear."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''can / be able to''. 살다 → 살 수 있었어요 = was able to survive.", "ex_ko": "이 덕분에 남성은 살 수 있었어요.", "ex_en": "Thanks to this, the man was able to survive."}, {"name": "~(으)로 (as)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Particle meaning ''as'' (a role or category). After a vowel or ㄹ it is 로: 일 → 일로 = as an event.", "ex_ko": "이 이야기는 전 세계 사람들에게 신기한 일로 알려졌어요.", "ex_en": "This story became known to people around the world as an amazing event."}, {"name": "~아/어지다 (passive)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Makes a verb passive. 알리다 ''to let know'' → 알려지다 ''to become known'' → 알려졌어요 = became known.", "ex_ko": "이 이야기는 전 세계 사람들에게 신기한 일로 알려졌어요.", "ex_en": "This story became known to people around the world as an amazing event."}, {"name": "~지 못하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Negative auxiliary meaning ''unable to'' or ''fail to''. Negation marker 지 + 못 (unable) + 하다.", "ex_ko": "때로는 예상하지 못한 것이 우리를 도와줄 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "Sometimes unexpected things can help us."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mortq85n4iry' and md5(translation) = '3ea7f2b036821a08126e9ea62d8bc1bc';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Something amusing happened in Canada. A baby beaver approached a person paddling a kayak.", "The baby beaver was very curious. It slowly circled around the kayak and observed the person carefully. It seemed as if it were thinking, \"What is this strange creature?\"", "The person paddling the kayak waited quietly. They didn''t move so the baby beaver wouldn''t be frightened. The two shared a peaceful moment together.", "This video became very popular on the internet. Many people left comments saying, \"So cute!\" and \"What a beautiful sight of nature and humans together.\" This special encounter with a small animal brought joy to people."], "sentences": [{"text": "캐나다에서 재미있는 일이 일어났어요.", "translation": "Something amusing happened in Canada.", "vocab": [{"ko": "재미있다", "en": "amusing, fun, interesting", "note": "Describes something that entertains or amuses"}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen, to occur", "note": "Common verb for events or situations"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~었어요", "exp": "Past tense in informal polite speech, indicating a completed action", "example_in_sentence": "일어났어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "아기 비버 한 마리가 카약(kayak, 작은 배) 타는 사람에게 다가왔습니다.", "translation": "A baby beaver approached a person paddling a kayak.", "vocab": [{"ko": "비버", "en": "beaver", "note": "Loanword; same pronunciation as English"}, {"ko": "한 마리", "en": "one (animal counter)", "note": "Native Korean counter for counting animals"}, {"ko": "다가오다", "en": "to approach, to come near", "note": "Implies movement toward someone or something"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~는 사람", "exp": "Present participle modifying a noun; describes the person in the act of paddling", "example_in_sentence": "카약 타는 사람"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "아기 비버는 호기심이 많았어요.", "translation": "The baby beaver was very curious.", "vocab": [{"ko": "호기심", "en": "curiosity, inquisitiveness", "note": "Noun describing the trait or state of being curious"}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many, abundant", "note": "Can mean ''much/a lot of'' when describing qualities"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~었어요", "exp": "Past tense in informal polite speech; describes a state or characteristic in the past", "example_in_sentence": "많았어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "카약 주변을 천천히 돌면서 사람을 자세히 관찰했습니다.", "translation": "It slowly circled around the kayak and observed the person carefully.", "vocab": [{"ko": "천천히", "en": "slowly, gradually", "note": "Adverb modifying verb actions"}, {"ko": "돌다", "en": "to circle, to turn around", "note": "Implies movement in a circular path"}, {"ko": "관찰하다", "en": "to observe, to watch closely", "note": "Formal term for careful observation"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~면서", "exp": "Connective showing two simultaneous or sequential actions by the same subject", "example_in_sentence": "돌면서 관찰했습니다"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "마치 \"이 이상한 생물체는 뭐지?\"라고 생각하는 것 같았어요.", "translation": "It seemed as if it were thinking, \"What is this strange creature?\"", "vocab": [{"ko": "마치", "en": "as if, just like", "note": "Adverb introducing a comparison or hypothetical situation"}, {"ko": "생물체", "en": "creature, organism, life form", "note": "Formal/scientific term for a living being"}, {"ko": "이상하다", "en": "to be strange, odd, unusual", "note": "Adjective describing something unfamiliar or peculiar"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~는 것 같다", "exp": "Expresses conjecture or appearance; ''it seems/appears that''", "example_in_sentence": "생각하는 것 같았어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "카약을 타던 사람은 조용히 기다렸어요.", "translation": "The person paddling the kayak waited quietly.", "vocab": [{"ko": "조용히", "en": "quietly, silently", "note": "Adverb describing manner of action"}, {"ko": "기다리다", "en": "to wait", "note": "Common verb for waiting patiently"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~던", "exp": "Past retrospective modifier; describes an ongoing or habitual action in the past", "example_in_sentence": "카약을 타던 사람"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "아기 비버가 무서워하지 않도록 움직이지 않았습니다.", "translation": "They didn''t move so the baby beaver wouldn''t be frightened.", "vocab": [{"ko": "무서워하다", "en": "to be frightened, to be afraid", "note": "Shows emotional reaction; ~하지 않도록 means ''so that it doesn''t''"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~지 않도록", "exp": "Negative purpose clause; ''so that/in order that (something) doesn''t happen''", "example_in_sentence": "무서워하지 않도록 움직이지 않았습니다"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "두 친구는 평화로운 시간을 보냈어요.", "translation": "The two shared a peaceful moment together.", "vocab": [{"ko": "평화롭다", "en": "to be peaceful; to be tranquil", "note": "Adjective describing a calm, undisturbed state"}, {"ko": "시간을 보내다", "en": "to spend time, to pass time", "note": "Collocation meaning to experience or use time"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 영상은 인터넷에서 큰 인기를 얻었어요.", "translation": "This video became very popular on the internet.", "vocab": [{"ko": "영상", "en": "video, footage, visual content", "note": "Formal term for recorded video material"}, {"ko": "인기를 얻다", "en": "to become popular, to gain popularity", "note": "Collocation meaning to achieve or receive popularity"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~었어요", "exp": "Past tense in informal polite speech; indicates a completed state change", "example_in_sentence": "얻었어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 \"너무 귀엽다\", \"자연과 사람이 함께하는 아름다운 모습\"이라고 댓글을 남겼습니다.", "translation": "Many people left comments saying, \"So cute!\" and \"What a beautiful sight of nature and humans together.\"", "vocab": [{"ko": "댓글을 남기다", "en": "to leave a comment", "note": "Collocation for posting comments on internet content"}, {"ko": "귀엽다", "en": "to be cute, adorable", "note": "Adjective describing something endearing"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~라고", "exp": "Quotation marker introducing what people said or thought", "example_in_sentence": "\"너무 귀엽다\"라고"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "작은 동물과의 특별한 만남이 사람들에게 기쁨을 주었어요.", "translation": "This special encounter with a small animal brought joy to people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "만남", "en": "encounter, meeting", "note": "Noun referring to coming together or meeting"}, {"ko": "기쁨을 주다", "en": "to bring joy, to give happiness", "note": "Collocation describing an action that causes joy"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}]}', vocab = '[{"ko": "재미있다", "en": "amusing, fun, interesting", "note": "Describes something that entertains or amuses"}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen, to occur", "note": "Common verb for events or situations"}, {"ko": "비버", "en": "beaver", "note": "Loanword; same pronunciation as English"}, {"ko": "한 마리", "en": "one (animal counter)", "note": "Native Korean counter for counting animals"}, {"ko": "다가오다", "en": "to approach, to come near", "note": "Implies movement toward someone or something"}, {"ko": "호기심", "en": "curiosity, inquisitiveness", "note": "Noun describing the trait or state of being curious"}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many, abundant", "note": "Can mean ''much/a lot of'' when describing qualities"}, {"ko": "천천히", "en": "slowly, gradually", "note": "Adverb modifying verb actions"}, {"ko": "돌다", "en": "to circle, to turn around", "note": "Implies movement in a circular path"}, {"ko": "관찰하다", "en": "to observe, to watch closely", "note": "Formal term for careful observation"}, {"ko": "마치", "en": "as if, just like", "note": "Adverb introducing a comparison or hypothetical situation"}, {"ko": "생물체", "en": "creature, organism, life form", "note": "Formal/scientific term for a living being"}, {"ko": "이상하다", "en": "to be strange, odd, unusual", "note": "Adjective describing something unfamiliar or peculiar"}, {"ko": "조용히", "en": "quietly, silently", "note": "Adverb describing manner of action"}, {"ko": "기다리다", "en": "to wait", "note": "Common verb for waiting patiently"}, {"ko": "무서워하다", "en": "to be frightened, to be afraid", "note": "Shows emotional reaction; ~하지 않도록 means ''so that it doesn''t''"}, {"ko": "평화롭다", "en": "to be peaceful; to be tranquil", "note": "Adjective describing a calm, undisturbed state"}, {"ko": "시간을 보내다", "en": "to spend time, to pass time", "note": "Collocation meaning to experience or use time"}, {"ko": "영상", "en": "video, footage, visual content", "note": "Formal term for recorded video material"}, {"ko": "인기를 얻다", "en": "to become popular, to gain popularity", "note": "Collocation meaning to achieve or receive popularity"}, {"ko": "댓글을 남기다", "en": "to leave a comment", "note": "Collocation for posting comments on internet content"}, {"ko": "귀엽다", "en": "to be cute, adorable", "note": "Adjective describing something endearing"}, {"ko": "만남", "en": "encounter, meeting", "note": "Noun referring to coming together or meeting"}, {"ko": "기쁨을 주다", "en": "to bring joy, to give happiness", "note": "Collocation describing an action that causes joy"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mos5lj0cbxli' and md5(translation) = '1c7e624151193c722cc3f30b0bc5da88';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["There is a spider called Dolomedes minor. This spider is also called a nursery web spider.", "The female spider builds a 15-centimeter-sized home for her babies. She takes care of the baby spiders there for 2 weeks.", "After 2 weeks, it''s time for the baby spiders to become independent. The babies make balloons out of spider silk.", "And they drift away on the wind to their new homes. It''s truly a fascinating story of a spider family."], "sentences": [{"text": "돌로메데스 미노르라는 거미가 있어요.", "translation": "There is a spider called Dolomedes minor.", "vocab": [{"ko": "거미", "en": "spider", "note": "Common noun; 거미줄 = spider web/silk"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~이 있어요", "exp": "Existence/presence statement in present tense, polite informal style.", "example_in_sentence": "거미가 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 거미는 육아 거미(nursery web spider)라고도 불러요.", "translation": "This spider is also called a nursery web spider.", "vocab": [], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~라고 불러요", "exp": "Passive/naming construction: ''is called X''; identifies an alternative name.", "example_in_sentence": "육아 거미라고도 불러요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "암컷 거미는 아기를 위해 15센티미터 크기의 집을 만들어요.", "translation": "The female spider builds a 15-centimeter-sized home for her babies.", "vocab": [{"ko": "암컷", "en": "female", "note": "Antonym: 수컷 (male)"}, {"ko": "크기", "en": "size", "note": "Noun; 크기의 = of [size]"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~을 위해", "exp": "Purpose or beneficiary marker; indicates ''for the sake of'' or ''on behalf of''.", "example_in_sentence": "아기를 위해"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 집에서 2주 동안 아기 거미들을 돌봐줘요.", "translation": "She takes care of the baby spiders there for 2 weeks.", "vocab": [{"ko": "동안", "en": "during; for (duration)", "note": "Marks a time period; 2주 동안 = for 2 weeks"}, {"ko": "돌봐주다", "en": "to take care of; to look after", "note": "~봐주다 emphasizes doing an action for someone else''s benefit"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~동안", "exp": "Duration marker; specifies how long an action or state continues.", "example_in_sentence": "2주 동안"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "2주가 지나면 아기 거미들은 독립할 시간이에요.", "translation": "After 2 weeks, it''s time for the baby spiders to become independent.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지나다", "en": "to pass; to go by", "note": "Temporal use: when time passes; 2주가 지나면 = after 2 weeks pass"}, {"ko": "독립하다", "en": "to become independent", "note": "~할 시간이에요 = it''s time to [verb]"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~면", "exp": "Conditional ''if/when''; introduces the condition or point in time when the main action occurs.", "example_in_sentence": "2주가 지나면"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "아기들은 거미줄로 풍선을 만들어요.", "translation": "The babies make balloons out of spider silk.", "vocab": [{"ko": "거미줄", "en": "spider web; spider silk", "note": "거미 (spider) + 줄 (thread/line)"}, {"ko": "풍선", "en": "balloon", "note": "Common noun; what the spiderlings create to drift"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그리고 바람을 타고 새로운 집으로 떠나가요.", "translation": "And they drift away on the wind to their new homes.", "vocab": [{"ko": "바람을 타다", "en": "to ride the wind; to drift on the wind", "note": "Idiomatic: 타다 = to ride/board"}, {"ko": "떠나가다", "en": "to depart; to go away", "note": "~아/어 가다 marks movement away from the speaker"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고", "exp": "Conjunction connecting two sequential or related actions: ''and then'' or ''and also''.", "example_in_sentence": "바람을 타고 새로운 집으로 떠나가요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "정말 신기한 거미 가족의 이야기예요.", "translation": "It''s truly a fascinating story of a spider family.", "vocab": [{"ko": "신기하다", "en": "fascinating; remarkable; amazing", "note": "Adjective describing something interesting or surprising"}, {"ko": "이야기", "en": "story; tale", "note": "Common noun; pairs with descriptive adjectives like 신기한"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ (attributive adjective)", "exp": "Adjective form modifying the following noun; 신기한 modifies 이야기.", "example_in_sentence": "신기한 거미 가족의 이야기"}], "analysis": []}]}', vocab = '[{"ko": "거미", "en": "spider", "note": "Common noun; 거미줄 = spider web/silk"}, {"ko": "암컷", "en": "female", "note": "Antonym: 수컷 (male)"}, {"ko": "크기", "en": "size", "note": "Noun; 크기의 = of [size]"}, {"ko": "동안", "en": "during; for (duration)", "note": "Marks a time period; 2주 동안 = for 2 weeks"}, {"ko": "돌봐주다", "en": "to take care of; to look after", "note": "~봐주다 emphasizes doing an action for someone else''s benefit"}, {"ko": "지나다", "en": "to pass; to go by", "note": "Temporal use: when time passes; 2주가 지나면 = after 2 weeks pass"}, {"ko": "독립하다", "en": "to become independent", "note": "~할 시간이에요 = it''s time to [verb]"}, {"ko": "거미줄", "en": "spider web; spider silk", "note": "거미 (spider) + 줄 (thread/line)"}, {"ko": "풍선", "en": "balloon", "note": "Common noun; what the spiderlings create to drift"}, {"ko": "바람을 타다", "en": "to ride the wind; to drift on the wind", "note": "Idiomatic: 타다 = to ride/board"}, {"ko": "떠나가다", "en": "to depart; to go away", "note": "~아/어 가다 marks movement away from the speaker"}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "fascinating; remarkable; amazing", "note": "Adjective describing something interesting or surprising"}, {"ko": "이야기", "en": "story; tale", "note": "Common noun; pairs with descriptive adjectives like 신기한"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mos5m9xwkjbx' and md5(translation) = '4d805240c1ccc6b81ced04775bc87483';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["According to recent research, great apes have complex theory of mind. Theory of Mind is the ability to understand the thoughts of other individuals. Great apes can engage in imaginative play just like humans. Great apes form complex relationships with each other and live together. They can also change their own thoughts when sufficient evidence appears. This behavior demonstrates high intelligence. In particular, a bonobo named Kanzi is famous. Kanzi can actually pretend to drink tea while playing. This is behavior that demonstrates imagination and creativity. These research results expand our understanding of animal intelligence. We can see that monkeys and humans are much more similar than we thought.", "Korean Teacher Shortage Becomes Serious, School Classes Disrupted", "What is an \"anxiety bag\"? A Popular Trend", "\"Talking Pig\" Becomes SNS Star", "United States and China Resume Talks Over Trade Issues", "Apple Significantly Improves iPhone Speed with New AI Chip"], "sentences": [{"text": "최근 연구에 따르면 유인원들이 복잡한 마음 이론을 가지고 있다고 해요.", "translation": "According to recent research, great apes have a complex theory of mind.", "vocab": [{"ko": "최근", "en": "recent; lately", "note": "Used with 연구, 뉴스, 트렌드 to mean ''recent'' or ''latest''"}, {"ko": "유인원", "en": "great ape", "note": "Includes chimpanzees, gorillas, bonobos, and orangutans"}, {"ko": "따르다", "en": "to follow; (에 따르면) according to", "note": "~에 따르면 means ''according to'' or ''based on''"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~에 따르면", "exp": "Introduces a source or basis for a statement; means ''according to'' or ''based on''", "example_in_sentence": "최근 연구에 따르면"}, {"pattern": "~다고 하다", "exp": "Reports indirect speech or claim; conveys hearsay or reported information", "example_in_sentence": "복잡한 마음 이론을 가지고 있다고 해요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "마음 이론(Theory of Mind)은 다른 개체의 생각을 이해하는 능력이에요.", "translation": "Theory of Mind is the ability to understand the thoughts of other individuals.", "vocab": [{"ko": "능력", "en": "ability; capacity", "note": "Often paired with 있다, 없다, or descriptive adjectives"}, {"ko": "이해하다", "en": "to understand; to comprehend", "note": "Takes direct object (ㄹ/을 object) or ~ 을/를 이해하다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~는 능력", "exp": "Relativizes a verb to modify a noun; ''~는 능력'' = ''the ability to ~''", "example_in_sentence": "다른 개체의 생각을 이해하는 능력"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "유인원들은 사람처럼 상상놀이도 할 수 있답니다.", "translation": "Great apes can engage in imaginative play just like humans.", "vocab": [{"ko": "상상놀이", "en": "imaginative play; pretend play", "note": "Compound noun: 상상(imagination) + 놀이(play)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~도 할 수 있다", "exp": "Expresses ability with the added meaning of ''also'' or ''even''; ''~도'' = ''also'', ''~ㄹ/을 수 있다'' = ''can''", "example_in_sentence": "상상놀이도 할 수 있답니다"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "유인원들은 서로 복잡한 관계를 맺고 살아가요.", "translation": "Great apes form complex relationships with each other and live together.", "vocab": [{"ko": "관계", "en": "relationship", "note": "~를/을 맺다 = ''to form a relationship''"}, {"ko": "맺다", "en": "to tie; to form; to establish", "note": "Often used with 관계 or 계약 to mean ''form'' or ''establish''"}, {"ko": "살아가다", "en": "to live; to get by; to go through life", "note": "More nuanced than 살다; implies ongoing daily life or journey"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 있다", "exp": "Indicates ongoing action or state; ''are ~ing'' or ''living and ~ing''", "example_in_sentence": "관계를 맺고 살아가요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "충분한 증거가 나타나면 자신의 생각을 바꾸기도 해요.", "translation": "They also change their minds when enough evidence appears.", "vocab": [{"ko": "증거", "en": "evidence; proof", "note": "Used in scientific, legal, or logical contexts"}, {"ko": "나타나다", "en": "to appear; to show up; to emerge", "note": "Passive sense of becoming visible or apparent"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~면", "exp": "Conditional form; ''if/when ~'' indicates a condition or circumstance", "example_in_sentence": "충분한 증거가 나타나면"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이런 행동은 높은 지능을 보여주는 것이에요.", "translation": "This behavior demonstrates high intelligence.", "vocab": [{"ko": "행동", "en": "behavior; action", "note": "Noun form; 행동하다 is the verb form"}, {"ko": "지능", "en": "intelligence", "note": "Used to describe mental ability or cognitive capacity"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~는 것이다", "exp": "Nominalization that asserts or explains; ''this is ~ing'' or ''this is the fact that ~''", "example_in_sentence": "높은 지능을 보여주는 것이에요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "특히 칸지라는 이름의 보노보 원숭이가 유명해요.", "translation": "In particular, a bonobo named Kanzi is famous.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특히", "en": "in particular; especially", "note": "Adverb that emphasizes or singles out something"}, {"ko": "보노보", "en": "bonobo", "note": "A type of great ape; also called pygmy chimpanzee"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "칸지는 실제로 차 마시는 흉내를 내며 놀 수 있어요.", "translation": "Kanzi can actually play by pretending to drink tea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "흉내", "en": "imitation; pretense; mimicry", "note": "~를/을 내다 = ''to imitate'' or ''to pretend''"}, {"ko": "실제로", "en": "actually; in reality; in fact", "note": "Adverb emphasizing that something truly happens, not just theoretically"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~으며 놀다", "exp": "Combines actions simultaneously; ''while ~ing, play'' or ''play while ~ing''", "example_in_sentence": "차 마시는 흉내를 내며 놀 수 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이는 상상력과 창의성을 보여주는 행동이에요.", "translation": "This is behavior that demonstrates imagination and creativity.", "vocab": [{"ko": "상상력", "en": "imagination; imaginative power", "note": "Noun form; 상상 is the simpler form meaning ''imagination''"}, {"ko": "창의성", "en": "creativity; creative ability", "note": "Formal noun; 창의적 is the adjective form"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~는 행동", "exp": "Relativizes a verb to modify a noun; ''the behavior that ~''", "example_in_sentence": "상상력과 창의성을 보여주는 행동"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이런 연구 결과는 동물의 지능에 대한 우리의 이해를 넓혀줘요.", "translation": "These research results expand our understanding of animal intelligence.", "vocab": [{"ko": "결과", "en": "result; outcome", "note": "Often paired with 연구, 조사, or 실험"}, {"ko": "넓혀주다", "en": "to expand; to broaden; to widen", "note": "~어/아 주다 adds sense of ''do for'' or benefit; 넓히다 is base form"}, {"ko": "이해", "en": "understanding; comprehension", "note": "Noun form; 이해하다 is the verb"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~에 대한", "exp": "Marks the target or object of a feeling, action, or thought; ''regarding'' or ''about''", "example_in_sentence": "동물의 지능에 대한 우리의 이해"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "원숭이와 인간이 생각보다 많이 비슷하다는 것을 알 수 있어요.", "translation": "We can see that monkeys and humans are much more similar than we thought.", "vocab": [{"ko": "생각보다", "en": "more than expected; more than one thought", "note": "Comparative; 생각(thought) + 보다(than) = ''than expected''"}, {"ko": "비슷하다", "en": "to be similar; to resemble", "note": "Adjective; 비슷하게 is adverb form"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~다는 것을 알 수 있다", "exp": "Expresses realization or discovery; ''we can see/understand that ~''", "example_in_sentence": "원숭이와 인간이 생각보다 많이 비슷하다는 것을 알 수 있어요"}], "analysis": []}]}', vocab = '[{"ko": "최근", "en": "recent; lately", "note": "Used with 연구, 뉴스, 트렌드 to mean ''recent'' or ''latest''"}, {"ko": "유인원", "en": "great ape", "note": "Includes chimpanzees, gorillas, bonobos, and orangutans"}, {"ko": "따르다", "en": "to follow; (에 따르면) according to", "note": "~에 따르면 means ''according to'' or ''based on''"}, {"ko": "능력", "en": "ability; capacity", "note": "Often paired with 있다, 없다, or descriptive adjectives"}, {"ko": "이해하다", "en": "to understand; to comprehend", "note": "Takes direct object (ㄹ/을 object) or ~ 을/를 이해하다"}, {"ko": "상상놀이", "en": "imaginative play; pretend play", "note": "Compound noun: 상상(imagination) + 놀이(play)"}, {"ko": "관계", "en": "relationship", "note": "~를/을 맺다 = ''to form a relationship''"}, {"ko": "맺다", "en": "to tie; to form; to establish", "note": "Often used with 관계 or 계약 to mean ''form'' or ''establish''"}, {"ko": "살아가다", "en": "to live; to get by; to go through life", "note": "More nuanced than 살다; implies ongoing daily life or journey"}, {"ko": "증거", "en": "evidence; proof", "note": "Used in scientific, legal, or logical contexts"}, {"ko": "나타나다", "en": "to appear; to show up; to emerge", "note": "Passive sense of becoming visible or apparent"}, {"ko": "행동", "en": "behavior; action", "note": "Noun form; 행동하다 is the verb form"}, {"ko": "지능", "en": "intelligence", "note": "Used to describe mental ability or cognitive capacity"}, {"ko": "특히", "en": "in particular; especially", "note": "Adverb that emphasizes or singles out something"}, {"ko": "보노보", "en": "bonobo", "note": "A type of great ape; also called pygmy chimpanzee"}, {"ko": "흉내", "en": "imitation; pretense; mimicry", "note": "~를/을 내다 = ''to imitate'' or ''to pretend''"}, {"ko": "실제로", "en": "actually; in reality; in fact", "note": "Adverb emphasizing that something truly happens, not just theoretically"}, {"ko": "상상력", "en": "imagination; imaginative power", "note": "Noun form; 상상 is the simpler form meaning ''imagination''"}, {"ko": "창의성", "en": "creativity; creative ability", "note": "Formal noun; 창의적 is the adjective form"}, {"ko": "결과", "en": "result; outcome", "note": "Often paired with 연구, 조사, or 실험"}, {"ko": "넓혀주다", "en": "to expand; to broaden; to widen", "note": "~어/아 주다 adds sense of ''do for'' or benefit; 넓히다 is base form"}, {"ko": "이해", "en": "understanding; comprehension", "note": "Noun form; 이해하다 is the verb"}, {"ko": "생각보다", "en": "more than expected; more than one thought", "note": "Comparative; 생각(thought) + 보다(than) = ''than expected''"}, {"ko": "비슷하다", "en": "to be similar; to resemble", "note": "Adjective; 비슷하게 is adverb form"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mos5mw8244wg' and md5(translation) = '8d292196981b7f2353dd9afe1efd2cd0';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "해외에서 재미있는 사건이 일어났어요.", "idx": 0, "translation": "An interesting incident happened overseas.", "vocab": [{"ko": "해외", "en": "overseas; abroad", "note": "한 + 밖 from Sino-Korean"}, {"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; event", "note": ""}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "아이들이 가짜 콧수염을 붙이고 나이 확인을 피해갔다는 뉴스가 화제가 되고 있어요.", "idx": 1, "translation": "News that children attached fake mustaches and avoided age verification is becoming a hot topic.", "vocab": [{"ko": "가짜", "en": "fake; counterfeit", "note": ""}, {"ko": "콧수염", "en": "mustache", "note": "콧 (nose) + 수염 (beard/whisker)"}, {"ko": "붙이다", "en": "to attach; to stick", "note": ""}, {"ko": "확인", "en": "confirmation; verification", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~다는 뉴스", "exp": "news that [reported content]", "example_in_sentence": "붙이고 나이 확인을 피해갔다는 뉴스"}, {"pattern": "~이 화제가 되다", "exp": "to become a hot topic", "example_in_sentence": "뉴스가 화제가 되고 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "온라인 서비스나 게임에서는 보통 나이를 확인해요.", "idx": 2, "translation": "Usually, online services and games verify age.", "vocab": [{"ko": "온라인", "en": "online", "note": ""}, {"ko": "서비스", "en": "service", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~보통", "exp": "usually; normally", "example_in_sentence": "보통 나이를 확인해요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "18세 미만은 사용할 수 없는 콘텐츠가 있기 때문이에요.", "idx": 3, "translation": "It is because there is content that cannot be used by those under 18 years old.", "vocab": [{"ko": "미만", "en": "under; less than", "note": "opposite of 이상 (and above)"}, {"ko": "콘텐츠", "en": "content", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~기 때문이다", "exp": "it is because; the reason is", "example_in_sentence": "있기 때문이에요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "하지만 일부 아이들이 창의적인 방법을 생각해냈어요.", "idx": 4, "translation": "However, some children came up with a creative method.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일부", "en": "some; part of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "창의적", "en": "creative", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생각해내다", "en": "to come up with; to devise", "note": "생각 + 내다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~지만", "exp": "however; but", "example_in_sentence": "하지만"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "아이들은 가짜 콧수염을 얼굴에 붙였어요.", "idx": 5, "translation": "The children attached fake mustaches to their faces.", "vocab": [{"ko": "얼굴", "en": "face", "note": ""}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그리고 카메라 앞에서 어른인 척했어요.", "idx": 6, "translation": "And they pretended to be adults in front of the camera.", "vocab": [{"ko": "카메라", "en": "camera", "note": ""}, {"ko": "어른", "en": "adult", "note": ""}, {"ko": "척하다", "en": "to pretend; to act as if", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~인 척하다", "exp": "to pretend to be; to act as if one is", "example_in_sentence": "어른인 척했어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "놀랍게도 일부 시스템에서는 이 방법이 통했다고 해요.", "idx": 7, "translation": "Surprisingly, this method reportedly worked on some systems.", "vocab": [{"ko": "놀랍게도", "en": "surprisingly; surprisingly enough", "note": "놀라다 + ~게도"}, {"ko": "시스템", "en": "system", "note": ""}, {"ko": "통하다", "en": "to work; to go through; to pass", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~다고 해요", "exp": "they say that; it is said that", "example_in_sentence": "통했다고 해요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 사건은 현재 나이 확인 시스템의 문제점을 보여줘요.", "idx": 8, "translation": "This incident shows the problems with the current age verification system.", "vocab": [{"ko": "현재", "en": "current; present", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시스템", "en": "system", "note": ""}, {"ko": "문제점", "en": "problem; weakness; issue", "note": "문제 + 점"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~을/를 보여주다", "exp": "to show; to demonstrate", "example_in_sentence": "문제점을 보여줘요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "기술이 발전해도 아직 완벽하지 않다는 뜻이에요.", "idx": 9, "translation": "It means that even though technology advances, it is still not perfect.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기술", "en": "technology; technique", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발전하다", "en": "to develop; to advance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "완벽하다", "en": "to be perfect", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~아/어도", "exp": "even if; even though", "example_in_sentence": "발전해도"}, {"pattern": "~다는 뜻이다", "exp": "it means that", "example_in_sentence": "완벽하지 않다는 뜻이에요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "앞으로 더 정확한 확인 방법이 필요할 것 같아요.", "idx": 10, "translation": "In the future, more accurate verification methods will likely be needed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "앞으로", "en": "in the future; ahead", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정확하다", "en": "to be accurate; to be precise", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방법", "en": "method; way", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~을/를 것 같다", "exp": "it seems that; it appears that; likely will", "example_in_sentence": "필요할 것 같아요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "전문가들은 이런 일이 한국에서도 일어날 수 있다고 말해요.", "idx": 11, "translation": "Experts say that this kind of thing could happen in Korea as well.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen; to occur", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~을/를 수 있다", "exp": "can; is possible to; may", "example_in_sentence": "일어날 수 있다고"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "부모님들은 자녀의 인터넷 사용을 더 주의 깊게 살펴봐야 할 것 같어요.", "idx": 12, "translation": "Parents will likely need to watch their children''s internet use more carefully.", "vocab": [{"ko": "부모님", "en": "parents", "note": "부모 + 님 (honorific)"}, {"ko": "자녀", "en": "child; children", "note": "formal/written form"}, {"ko": "인터넷", "en": "internet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주의 깊다", "en": "to be careful; to be attentive", "note": "주의 + 깊다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~을/를 것 같다", "exp": "it seems that; likely will", "example_in_sentence": "살펴봐야 할 것 같아요"}], "analysis": []}], "version": "p3"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "해외", "en": "overseas; abroad", "note": "한 + 밖 from Sino-Korean"}, {"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; event", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가짜", "en": "fake; counterfeit", "note": ""}, {"ko": "콧수염", "en": "mustache", "note": "콧 (nose) + 수염 (beard/whisker)"}, {"ko": "붙이다", "en": "to attach; to stick", "note": ""}, {"ko": "확인", "en": "confirmation; verification", "no